var e={"p ← partition(a)        // as in quick sort":`p ← partition(a)        // 和快速排序一样`,"if p = k: return a[p]":`如果 p = k: 返回 a[p]`,"if k < p:":`如果 k < p:`,"return select(the part before p, k)":`返回 select(p 之前的部分, k)`,"return select(the part after p, k)":`返回 select(p 之后的部分, k)`,"One item, not the whole order":`一项，而不是整个顺序`,"Which is the 2nd smallest of these? Or the median? You could sort the row and read off the cell, but that does far more work than the question asks for.":`这些数中第 2 小的是哪个？或者中位数？你可以把这一排排好序再读出那个格子，但那样做的工作远超问题所需。`,"In a sorted row the 2nd smallest sits in cell 1. The only thing that matters is what ends up in that one cell.":`在排好序的一排里，第 2 小的在格子 1。唯一重要的是最后落在那一个格子里的是什么。`,"what belongs here?":`这里该放什么？`,"Looking for":`要找的是`,"the 2nd smallest":`第 2 小的`,"cell 1":`格子 1`,"Pivot landed in":`基准落在`,"Still searching":`仍在搜索`,"cells 0 to 7":`格子 0 到 7`,"Items looked at":`查看过的项`,"Partition once":`划分一次`,"Do one quick sort partition around the last item, 4. Smaller items go to its left, bigger to its right, and 4 drops into cell 3.":`围绕最后一项 4 做一次快速排序的划分。更小的项去它左边，更大的去右边，4 落到格子 3。`,"That is 4’s final cell. So 4 is the 4th smallest, without anything having been sorted.":`那是 4 的最终位置。所以 4 是第 4 小的，而什么都还没排序。`,"the 4th smallest":`第 4 小的`,"cell 3":`格子 3`,"Throw one side away":`扔掉一边`,"Cell 1 is to the left of cell 3. So the answer is one of the three items on the left.":`格子 1 在格子 3 的左边。所以答案是左边三项之一。`,"Quick sort would now sort <em>both</em> sides. Quickselect drops the right side for good: five items it will never look at again.":`快速排序这时会把<em>两边</em>都排好。快速选择则永久丢掉右边：五个它再也不会看的项。`,"it is in here":`在这里面`,"cells 0 to 2":`格子 0 到 2`,"Partition what is left":`划分剩下的`,"Same again on those three, around the last one, 1. Nothing is smaller, so 1 swaps into cell 0.":`对这三项再做一次，围绕最后一项 1。没有更小的，所以 1 交换到格子 0。`,"Cell 1 is to its right this time. Two items left.":`这次格子 1 在它右边。剩下两项。`,"cell 0":`格子 0`,"cells 1 to 2":`格子 1 到 2`,"The pivot lands on the cell":`基准落在了那个格子上`,"Partition the last two around 2. It swaps into cell 1: exactly the cell being asked about.":`围绕 2 划分最后两项。它交换到格子 1：正好是问的那个格子。`,"The 2nd smallest is 2. The right side of the row is still a jumble, and it does not matter.":`第 2 小的是 2。这一排的右边还是乱的，但这无所谓。`,"2nd smallest":`第 2 小的`,found:`找到了`,"Half the work each time":`每次只做一半的工作`,"Each round looks only at what survived the last: 8 items, then 3, then 2. On average the pile halves, and n + n/2 + n/4 + … never reaches 2n.":`每一轮只看上一轮留下来的：8 项，然后 3 项，然后 2 项。平均下来，剩下的每次减半，而 n + n/2 + n/4 + … 永远不会达到 2n。`,"Like quick sort, a run of bad pivots makes it slow. Picking the pivot at random makes that very unlikely.":`和快速排序一样，一连串糟糕的基准会让它变慢。随机选基准能让这非常不可能发生。`,"O(n) on average, against O(n log n) to sort first. O(n²) at worst.":`平均 O(n)，而先排序要 O(n log n)。最坏 O(n²)。`,"Sorting would have looked at about 24.":`排序的话大约要看 24 次。`},t={"subsets(items, chosen so far):":`subsets(items, chosen):`,"if no items are left:":`如果 没有剩下的项:`,"record chosen":`记录 chosen`,"take the next item":`取下一项`,"subsets(the rest, chosen + that item)":`subsets(其余的, chosen + 这一项)`,"put it back                    // undo the choice":`把它放回去                    // 撤销这个选择`,"subsets(the rest, chosen)":`subsets(其余的, chosen)`,"Choices made":`已做的选择`,"Every possible choice":`每一种可能的选择`,"List every subset of A, B, C: every way of choosing some, all or none of them. Many problems come down to this: try every combination, and keep the ones that work.":`列出 A、B、C 的每个子集：选其中一些、全部或一个都不选的每一种方式。很多问题都归结于此：试遍每种组合，留下行得通的。`,"<strong>Backtracking</strong> is the organised way to do it. Start with nothing chosen.":`<strong>回溯</strong>是有条理地做这件事的方法。从什么都没选开始。`,"nothing chosen yet":`还什么都没选`,"Items decided":`已决定的项`,"of A, B, C":`/ A、B、C`,"Subsets found":`已找到的子集`,"One decision at a time":`一次一个决定`,Choose:`选择`,"Take the first item and make one decision about it: is A in, or out? Each answer leads somewhere different.":`取第一项，对它做一个决定：A 要还是不要？每个回答都通向不同的地方。`,"Going left means taking it. Going right means leaving it.":`往左表示要它。往右表示不要它。`,"A tree of choices":`一棵选择树`,"From each of those, decide about B in the same way. Then C. Every decision doubles the number of ways things could have gone.":`对每个分支，用同样的方式决定 B。然后是 C。每个决定都让可能的走向翻倍。`,"The leaves are the answers":`叶子就是答案`,"After three decisions there is nothing left to decide. Each leaf is one complete set of choices: one subset. There are eight, from ABC to the empty set.":`三个决定之后，就没有什么要决定的了。每片叶子都是一组完整的选择：一个子集。一共八个，从 ABC 到空集。`,"No subset is missed and none appears twice, because every leaf is reached by a different run of decisions.":`没有子集被遗漏，也没有出现两次的，因为每片叶子都是由一串不同的决定到达的。`,"Walking it: go back and try again":`走一遍：退回去再试`,"The tree is never built in memory. A recursive function walks it depth first: go down taking items until a leaf, record it, then step <strong>back</strong> one decision, undo it, and take the other branch.":`这棵树从来不会在内存中构建出来。一个递归函数深度优先地走它：一路取项往下走到一片叶子，记录下来，然后<strong>退回</strong>一个决定，撤销它，走另一个分支。`,"That step back is the backtrack. Only the current path is ever held.":`那一步退回就是回溯。任何时候只保存当前的路径。`,"n items have 2ⁿ subsets. Backtracking pays off when whole branches can be ruled out early, as in the next lesson.":`n 个项有 2ⁿ 个子集。当整个分支能被提前排除时，回溯才划算，就像下一课那样。`,"Numbered in the order they are reached.":`按到达的顺序编号。`},n={"if nothing is unused:":`如果 没有未使用的:`,"record the arrangement":`记录 这个排列`,"for each item in unused:":`对每个 unused 中的项:`,"move it onto the end of arrangement   // choose":`把它移到 arrangement 的末尾   // 选择`,"permute(arrangement, the rest)        // explore":`permute(arrangement, 其余的)        // 探索`,"move it back                          // un-choose":`把它移回去                          // 撤销选择`,Arrangements:`排列`,"Every possible order":`每一种可能的顺序`,"Three letters wait in the row behind. In how many different orders can they be laid out in front? Each order is a <strong>permutation</strong>.":`后面一排有三个字母在等着。它们在前面能排成多少种不同的顺序？每种顺序都是一个<strong>排列</strong>。`,"There are 3 choices for the first place, 2 left for the second, 1 for the third: 3 × 2 × 1 = 6. The job is to produce all six without missing or repeating one.":`第一个位置有 3 种选择，第二个剩 2 种，第三个 1 种：3 × 2 × 1 = 6。任务是把六种全部列出来，不漏也不重复。`,"Found so far":`目前已找到`,"Choose, then choose again":`选择，再选择`,"Fill the places from the left, always taking the first unused letter. A goes first. Of what is left, B goes second. Only C remains for the third.":`从左往右填位置，每次都取第一个未使用的字母。A 排第一。剩下的里面，B 排第二。第三个只剩 C 了。`,"Nothing is unused, so this is a complete arrangement: A B C.":`没有未使用的了，所以这是一个完整的排列：A B C。`,"Undo the last choices":`撤销最后的选择`,"To get a different arrangement, take the last choice back. C comes off, but it was the only option for the third place. So B comes off too.":`要得到不同的排列，就收回最后一个选择。C 拿下来，但它是第三个位置唯一的选项。所以 B 也拿下来。`,"A stays where it is. The second place still has one option that has not been tried: C.":`A 留在原处。第二个位置还有一个没试过的选项：C。`,"B is done here: try C":`B 在这里已试过：试 C`,"Try the next option":`试下一个选项`,"C goes second this time, and B is all that is left for the third. A C B.":`这次 C 排第二，第三个只剩 B。A C B。`,"That is everything that starts with A.":`以 A 开头的就是这些了。`,"Back all the way":`一路退回去`,"Both options for the second place have been used, so the search backs up past it. Even A comes off.":`第二个位置的两个选项都用过了，所以搜索退过它。连 A 也拿下来了。`,"The first place has two options it has not tried yet.":`第一个位置还有两个没试过的选项。`,"A is done here: try B":`A 在这里已试过：试 B`,"A new first letter":`新的第一个字母`,"B goes first. The rest goes exactly as before, on the letters that are left: A then C gives B A C, and backing up one gives B C A.":`B 排第一。剩下的完全和之前一样，用剩下的字母来排：A 然后 C 得到 B A C，退回一步得到 B C A。`,"B C A comes next.":`接下来是 B C A。`,"Choose, explore, un-choose":`选择、探索、撤销选择`,"With C first come C A B and C B A, and the search is over: six arrangements, each found once.":`C 排第一时得到 C A B 和 C B A，搜索结束：六个排列，每个只找到一次。`,"This is the whole shape of backtracking. Make a choice, follow it as far as it goes, then put things back exactly as they were and make the next choice.":`这就是回溯的完整形状。做一个选择，顺着它走到底，然后把东西原样放回去，再做下一个选择。`,"n! arrangements. 10 items make 3.6 million; 15 make over a trillion.":`n! 个排列。10 个项有 360 万个；15 个就超过一万亿个。`},r={"if square is the exit: return yes":`如果 square 是出口: 返回 是`,"put square on the trail":`把 square 放到足迹上`,"for each neighbour: right, forward, left, back:":`对每个 邻居，按右、前、左、后:`,"if it is open and not on the trail:":`如果 它是通的且不在足迹上:`,"if solve(neighbour): return yes":`如果 solve(neighbour): 返回 是`,"take square off the trail      // dead end":`把 square 从足迹上拿下      // 死路`,"The walk":`行走`,"A way through":`一条出路`,"The plain blocks are walls. A walker stands on square 1 at the back-left and has to reach the exit at the front-right, moving one square at a time.":`普通的方块是墙。一个行走者站在左后方的 1 号格子上，要一次走一格，到达右前方的出口。`,"It cannot see the maze from above. All it can do is try a direction and find out.":`它没法从上方俯瞰迷宫。它能做的只是试一个方向，看看结果。`,exit:`出口`,Trail:`足迹`,squares:`格`,"Squares stepped on":`走过的格子`,"Backed out of":`退出来的`,"Pick an order and keep to it":`选一个顺序并坚持下去`,"The rule: at every square try <strong>right</strong> first, then forward, then left, then back. Take the first way that is open, and leave a numbered marker on each square.":`规则是：在每个格子上先试<strong>右</strong>，然后前，然后左，然后后。走第一条通的路，并在每个格子上留一个带编号的标记。`,"Right is open three times running. Then there is a wall ahead and nothing new on any side.":`右边连续三次都是通的。然后前方是墙，各个方向都没有新路了。`,"dead end":`死路`,"Back up to the last choice":`退回到上一个选择`,"Pick up marker 4 and step back. Square 3 has no other way out either, so pick that up too.":`捡起 4 号标记，退一步。3 号格子也没有别的出路，所以把它也捡起来。`,"Square 2 is different. Right has been tried, but <strong>forward</strong> has not, and it is open.":`2 号格子不一样。右边已经试过了，但<strong>前</strong>还没试，而且是通的。`,"forward is untried":`前还没试过`,"Carry on from there":`从那里继续`,"Forward, and forward again. Now right is open once more, and right is always tried first.":`往前，再往前。现在右边又通了，而右边总是先试。`,"The markers are numbered 3, 4, 5: the old 3 and 4 were picked up, so the trail only ever shows the way that is still alive.":`标记的编号是 3、4、5：旧的 3 和 4 被捡起来了，所以足迹只显示仍然活着的那条路。`,Out:`出去了`,"A wall to the right, so forward. Then right, onto the exit.":`右边是墙，所以往前。然后往右，走到出口上。`,"The trail left on the floor is the route: seven squares, start to finish. The dead end is not part of it.":`留在地上的足迹就是路线：七个格子，从起点到终点。死路不是它的一部分。`,"The same search everywhere":`到处都是同样的搜索`,"The trail is the recursion stack: each marker is one call still waiting for an answer. Picking a marker up is that call returning “no”.":`足迹就是递归栈：每个标记都是一次仍在等答案的调用。捡起一个标记，就是那次调用返回了“否”。`,"Sudoku is the same search with digits in place of directions: write one in, carry on, and if a square has no digit left to try, rub out the last one and try the next.":`数独是同样的搜索，只是用数字代替方向：填一个进去，继续；如果某个格子没有数字可试了，就擦掉上一个，试下一个。`,"This finds a way out, not the shortest. For the shortest, use breadth-first search.":`这找到的是一条出路，而不是最短的。要最短的，就用广度优先搜索。`,"One square, row 2 column 0, was never visited.":`有一个格子，第 2 行第 0 列，从没被访问过。`},i={"if n < 2: return n":`如果 n < 2: 返回 n`,"if memo has n: return memo[n]      // seen it before":`如果 memo 里有 n: 返回 memo[n]      // 以前见过`,"memo[n] ← answer                   // write it down":`memo[n] ← answer                   // 把它记下来`,"return answer":`返回 answer`,"What is remembered":`记住了什么`,"A recursion that branches":`会分叉的递归`,"Each Fibonacci number is the sum of the two before it: fib(n) = fib(n − 1) + fib(n − 2). Written as a recursive function, every call makes two more.":`每个斐波那契数都是前两个数的和：fib(n) = fib(n − 1) + fib(n − 2)。写成递归函数，每次调用都会再发起两次调用。`,"Here is every call made to work out fib(4). Each node is one call, labelled with its n. Nine calls, for a very small number.":`这里是算 fib(4) 时发起的每一次调用。每个节点是一次调用，标着它的 n。九次调用，就为了一个很小的数。`,Memo:`备忘录`,"The same work, twice":`同样的工作做了两遍`,"Look at the two calls for fib(2). They are the same question, and each works out the same answer from scratch, with its own calls below it.":`看看两次 fib(2) 调用。它们是同一个问题，而每次都从头算出同样的答案，各自下面还有自己的调用。`,"It gets worse quickly. fib(5) repeats the whole of fib(3) twice. fib(40) makes over 300 million calls, nearly all of them repeats.":`情况很快就变得更糟。fib(5) 把整个 fib(3) 重复了两次。fib(40) 要发起三亿多次调用，几乎全是重复。`,"About 1.6 times as many calls for each step up in n: exponential.":`n 每增加 1，调用次数大约变成 1.6 倍：指数级。`,"worked out again":`又算了一遍`,"fib(2) is worked out twice, fib(1) three times.":`fib(2) 算了两次，fib(1) 算了三次。`,"Write the answers down":`把答案记下来`,"The fix is almost embarrassingly simple. The first time a call finishes, save its answer in a table, the <strong>memo</strong>, under its n.":`修正方法简单得几乎让人不好意思。一次调用第一次完成时，就把它的答案按 n 存进一张表，也就是<strong>备忘录</strong>。`,"Follow the left side down and back up: fib(2) is 1, then fib(3) is 2. Both are now written down.":`沿左边往下走再回来：fib(2) 是 1，然后 fib(3) 是 2。两个现在都记下来了。`,"Look it up instead":`改为查表`,"Now the right side asks for fib(2) again. Before doing any work, check the memo: the answer is already there.":`现在右边又要 fib(2)。在做任何工作之前，先查备忘录：答案已经在那里了。`,"That call returns at once, and the calls it would have made never happen. A whole subtree is gone.":`那次调用立刻返回，它原本会发起的调用都不会发生。整棵子树都没了。`,"from the memo":`来自备忘录`,"Each question once":`每个问题只算一次`,"fib(4) is 2 + 1 = 3, from seven calls instead of nine. The saving grows fast: with a memo, fib(40) takes 79 calls, not 300 million.":`fib(4) 是 2 + 1 = 3，用了七次调用而不是九次。节省得越来越多：有了备忘录，fib(40) 只要 79 次调用，而不是三亿次。`,"This is <strong>dynamic programming</strong>, top-down: ordinary recursion, plus a table so that no subproblem is solved twice.":`这就是自顶向下的<strong>动态规划</strong>：普通的递归，加上一张表，让任何子问题都不会被解两次。`,"O(n): there are only n + 1 different questions, and each is answered once.":`O(n)：只有 n + 1 个不同的问题，每个只回答一次。`,"When it works":`什么时候管用`,Recognise:`识别`,"Memoization pays off when two things are true. The problem breaks into smaller problems of the same kind. And those smaller problems <em>overlap</em>: the same ones come up again and again.":`两件事都成立时，记忆化才划算。问题能拆成同类的更小问题。并且这些更小的问题会<em>重叠</em>：同样的问题一再出现。`,"Fibonacci has both. Merge sort has only the first: its halves never repeat, so there is nothing to remember.":`斐波那契两样都有。归并排序只有第一样：它的两半从不重复，所以没什么要记的。`,"A recursion that keeps asking the same questions wants a memo.":`一个不断问同样问题的递归，需要一个备忘录。`,"Overlapping subproblems are the sign.":`重叠子问题就是信号。`},a={"for i from 2 to n:":`对于 i 从 2 到 n:`,"return table[n]":`返回 table[n]`,"The table":`表`,"Start from the bottom":`从底部开始`,"Memoization starts with the big question and works down, saving answers as it goes. <strong>Tabulation</strong> turns that round: answer the smallest questions first, and build up.":`记忆化从大问题开始往下做，边做边保存答案。<strong>制表法</strong>反过来：先回答最小的问题，再一步步往上搭。`,"There is no recursion. There is just a table, with one cell for each subproblem, filled in an order that makes sure everything a cell needs is already there.":`没有递归。只有一张表，每个子问题一个格子，按一定顺序填写，保证每个格子需要的东西都已经在那里了。`,Additions:`加法次数`,"One cell for each of fib(0) to fib(7).":`fib(0) 到 fib(7) 各一个格子。`,"The base cases":`基本情况`,"Two answers need no working out: fib(0) is 0 and fib(1) is 1. Write them in.":`有两个答案不需要算：fib(0) 是 0，fib(1) 是 1。把它们填进去。`,"These are the same base cases the recursion had. Here they are simply where the table starts.":`这些就是递归里的那些基本情况。在这里，它们只是表开始的地方。`,"Each from the two before":`每个都由前两个得出`,"fib(2) is fib(1) + fib(0). Both are already in the table, so it is one addition: 1.":`fib(2) 是 fib(1) + fib(0)。两个都已经在表里了，所以只是一次加法：1。`,"Nothing was called and nothing was looked for. The two cells to its left were simply read.":`没有调用任何东西，也没有查找任何东西。只是读了它左边的两个格子。`,"Left to right":`从左到右`,"Carry on along the row. Each new cell reads its two neighbours on the left and adds them: 2, then 3, then 5.":`沿着这一排继续。每个新格子读取它左边的两个邻居并相加：2，然后 3，然后 5。`,"The order matters. Going left to right means a cell is never read before it has been written.":`顺序很重要。从左到右意味着一个格子永远不会在被写入之前被读取。`,"The answer is the last cell":`答案在最后一个格子`,"Two more and the table is full: fib(7) is 13.":`再填两个，表就满了：fib(7) 是 13。`,"Eight cells, six additions. The recursive version, with nothing saved, makes 41 calls to get the same number.":`八个格子，六次加法。不保存任何东西的递归版本，要发起 41 次调用才能得到同一个数。`,"O(n) time: one pass along the table, constant work per cell.":`O(n) 时间：沿着表走一趟，每个格子的工作量是常数。`,"Keep only what you need":`只保留需要的`,Refine:`精简`,"Look at what each cell actually read: only the two before it. Everything further left is never used again.":`看看每个格子实际读了什么：只有它前面的两个。更左边的一切再也不会被用到。`,"So the whole table can be replaced by two variables. Seeing which cells are still needed is something a table makes easy, and recursion hides.":`所以整张表可以换成两个变量。哪些格子还需要，用表来看一目了然，用递归就看不出来。`,"Memo or table?":`备忘录还是表？`,"Same idea, same speed. The table avoids deep recursion; the memo only solves the subproblems it meets.":`同样的思路，同样的速度。表避免了很深的递归；备忘录只解它遇到的子问题。`,"Memory: O(1) instead of O(n).":`内存：O(1) 而不是 O(n)。`},o={"for each item i, of weight w and value v:":`对每个 物品 i，重量为 w，价值为 v:`,"for c from 0 to capacity:":`对于 c 从 0 到 capacity:`,"if w ≤ c: take ← v + best[i − 1][c − w]":`如果 w ≤ c: take ← v + best[i − 1][c − w]`,"best[i][c] ← the larger of leave and take":`best[i][c] ← leave 和 take 中较大的`,"return best[last item][capacity]":`返回 best[最后一个物品][capacity]`,"The items":`物品`,"What to pack":`装什么`,"A bag holds 5 kg. There are three items, each with a weight and a value, and each can be taken once or left behind. Which choice is worth the most?":`一个包能装 5 kg。有三个物品，每个都有重量和价值，每个可以拿一次或者不拿。哪种选择价值最高？`,"Trying every combination doubles with each item. Instead, ask a smaller question many times: <em>the best from the first few items, in a bag of a given size</em>. The table has a cell for each. With no items, the answer is 0 for every size.":`试遍每种组合，每多一个物品就翻一倍。换个办法，多次问一个更小的问题：<em>只用前几个物品，在给定大小的包里能得到的最好结果</em>。表格为每个这样的问题准备了一个格子。没有物品时，任何大小的答案都是 0。`,"Item A":`物品 A`,"worth 3":`价值 3`,"Item B":`物品 B`,"worth 4":`价值 4`,"Item C":`物品 C`,"worth 5":`价值 5`,"The bag holds":`包能装`,"One item":`一个物品`,"Now allow item A: 2 kg, worth 3. In a bag of 0 or 1 kg it does not fit, so the best is still 0.":`现在允许用物品 A：2 kg，价值 3。在 0 或 1 kg 的包里装不下，所以最好的仍然是 0。`,"From 2 kg upwards it fits, and taking it is better than nothing: 3 all the way along.":`从 2 kg 开始就装得下了，拿它总比什么都没有好：一路都是 3。`,"A fits: worth 3":`A 装得下：价值 3`,"Take it or leave it":`拿还是不拿`,"Add item B (3 kg, worth 4), and look at the 5 kg bag. Two choices. <strong>Leave</strong> B: the answer is the cell above, 3. <strong>Take</strong> B: that is 4, plus the best that fits in the 2 kg left over, which the row above already knows: 3.":`加上物品 B（3 kg，价值 4），看看 5 kg 的包。两个选择。<strong>不拿</strong> B：答案是上面的格子，3。<strong>拿</strong> B：那是 4，再加上剩下的 2 kg 里能装的最好结果，而上一行已经知道了：3。`,"4 + 3 = 7 beats 3. Every cell in the table is filled by this same comparison.":`4 + 3 = 7 胜过 3。表里的每个格子都是由同样的比较填出来的。`,"The last row":`最后一行`,"Item C is 4 kg, worth 5. In the 5 kg bag, taking it leaves 1 kg, and the best for 1 kg is 0: so 5 in total. Leaving it keeps the 7 above.":`物品 C 是 4 kg，价值 5。在 5 kg 的包里，拿它会剩下 1 kg，而 1 kg 最好是 0：所以总共 5。不拿它就保留上面的 7。`,"7 wins. The bottom-right cell is the answer to the whole problem.":`7 胜出。右下角的格子就是整个问题的答案。`,"Each row only ever reads the row above it.":`每一行只会读取它上面的那一行。`,"Which items, though?":`那么是哪些物品？`,"The table gives the value. To find the items, walk back from the answer. If a cell equals the one above it, that item was left. If not, it was taken: move up a row and left by its weight.":`表给出的是价值。要找出物品，就从答案往回走。如果一个格子等于它上面的格子，那个物品就没拿。如果不等，就是拿了：往上移一行，再往左移它的重量那么多。`,"7 equals the 7 above: C was left. That 7 differs from the 3 above it: B was taken, leaving 2 kg. And 3 differs from 0: A was taken.":`7 等于上面的 7：C 没拿。那个 7 不同于它上面的 3：B 拿了，剩下 2 kg。而 3 不同于 0：A 拿了。`,"pack A and B":`装 A 和 B`,"A and B: 5 kg, worth 7.":`A 和 B：5 kg，价值 7。`,"What it cost":`代价是多少`,"Three items and six bag sizes: 24 cells, each one comparison. With 100 items and a 1,000 kg bag it is 100,000 cells, where trying every combination would never finish.":`三个物品，六种包的大小：24 个格子，每个一次比较。有 100 个物品和一个 1,000 kg 的包时，就是 100,000 个格子，而试遍每种组合永远也做不完。`,"This shape, a table over “how much of the input” and “how much room”, turns up in budgeting, cutting stock, and scheduling.":`这种形状，一张以“用了多少输入”和“还有多少空间”为维度的表，在做预算、切割材料和排程中都会出现。`,"O(items × capacity) in time and space; one row of space if only the value is wanted.":`时间和空间都是 O(物品数 × 容量)；如果只要价值，空间只需一行。`},s={"for i from 1 to length of a:":`对于 i 从 1 到 a 的长度:`,"for j from 1 to length of b:":`对于 j 从 1 到 b 的长度:`,"same[i][j] ← the larger of":`same[i][j] ← 以下两者中较大的`,"same[i − 1][j] and same[i][j − 1]":`same[i − 1][j] 和 same[i][j − 1]`,"return same[last i][last j]":`返回 same[最后的 i][最后的 j]`,"What two sequences share":`两个序列有什么共同点`,"How alike are TAN and ANTS? One measure is their <strong>longest common subsequence</strong>: the longest run of letters that appears in both, in the same order, though not necessarily side by side. Here it is AN.":`TAN 和 ANTS 有多像？一种衡量方法是它们的<strong>最长公共子序列</strong>：在两者中都出现、顺序相同但不一定相邻的最长字母串。这里是 AN。`,"The table asks the question of every pair of beginnings: a row for each start of TAN, a column for each start of ANTS. Against an empty word, nothing is shared: 0.":`这张表对每一对开头部分都问这个问题：TAN 的每个开头部分占一行，ANTS 的每个开头部分占一列。和空词相比，没有任何共同点：0。`,"File comparison, spell checking, matching DNA.":`文件比较、拼写检查、DNA 比对。`,"First word":`第一个词`,"Second word":`第二个词`,"When the letters match":`字母相同时`,"Row T. Against A and against AN, T matches nothing: 0. Against ANT, the last letters are the same: T and T.":`T 行。和 A、AN 相比，T 什么都不匹配：0。和 ANT 相比，最后的字母相同：T 和 T。`,"A match extends whatever the two words shared <em>before</em> those letters. That is the cell up and to the left, plus one: 0 + 1.":`一次匹配会延续两个词在这些字母<em>之前</em>共有的东西。那就是左上方的格子，再加一：0 + 1。`,"When they differ":`字母不同时`,"Row TA, column A: a match again, so 1. Now the next cell, TA against AN. The last letters, A and N, differ, so one of them is no help.":`TA 行，A 列：又是匹配，所以是 1。现在是下一个格子，TA 对 AN。最后的字母 A 和 N 不同，所以其中一个没有帮助。`,"Drop one or the other and take the better result: the cell above, or the cell to the left. Here, 1.":`去掉其中一个，取较好的结果：上面的格子，或者左边的格子。这里是 1。`,"Fill the table":`填满这张表`,"Row TAN. Against AN, N matches N, and before those letters the words shared 1: so 2. After that the letters differ, and the 2 is carried along.":`TAN 行。和 AN 相比，N 匹配 N，而在这些字母之前两个词共有 1：所以是 2。之后字母不同，2 一直被带下去。`,"The bottom-right cell covers both whole words. The longest common subsequence has length 2.":`右下角的格子涵盖两个完整的词。最长公共子序列的长度是 2。`,"Read the letters back":`把字母读回来`,"To recover the letters, walk back from the corner. Where the letters differ, step to whichever neighbour holds the same number. Where they match, that letter is part of the answer: step diagonally.":`要找回这些字母，就从角上往回走。字母不同的地方，走到存着相同数字的那个邻居。字母相同的地方，这个字母就是答案的一部分：沿对角线走。`,"The walk passes two matches, N and then A. Read in order: AN.":`这条路经过两次匹配，先是 N，然后是 A。按顺序读：AN。`,"A, then N":`A，然后 N`,"One pattern, many problems":`一个模式，很多问题`,"Twenty cells, each filled by looking at three neighbours. Comparing every subsequence of one word with the other would double with every letter.":`二十个格子，每个都是看三个邻居填出来的。把一个词的每个子序列都和另一个词比较，每多一个字母就要翻倍。`,"Change the rule in the cell and the same table measures other things: the fewest edits to turn one word into another, or the best way to line up two genes.":`改变格子里的规则，同一张表就能衡量别的东西：把一个词变成另一个词最少要改几次，或者对齐两个基因的最佳方式。`,"Longest common subsequence: AN.":`最长公共子序列：AN。`},c={"return bit k of set is on":`返回 set 的第 k 位是否开着`,"switch bit k on":`打开第 k 位`,"return a AND b":`返回 a AND b`,"return a OR b":`返回 a OR b`,"return a AND (NOT b)":`返回 a AND (NOT b)`,"The sets":`集合`,"A set in a single number":`一个数里的集合`,"To store a set of small numbers, give every possible member one bit: on if it is in the set, off if it is not. The cells are numbered 7 down to 0.":`要存一个由小数字组成的集合，就给每个可能的成员一位：在集合里就开着，不在就关着。格子从 7 往下编号到 0。`,"This row is the set {1, 3, 4}. Is 3 in it? Look at bit 3. No hashing, and no searching.":`这一排就是集合 {1, 3, 4}。3 在里面吗？看第 3 位。不用哈希，也不用搜索。`,"3 is in the set":`3 在集合里`,"contains 3?":`包含 3？`,"Add, remove, look up":`添加、删除、查找`,"These are the mask operations again. Adding 6 means switching bit 6 on. Removing a member switches its bit off. Asking is testing a bit.":`这些又是掩码操作。添加 6 就是打开第 6 位。删除一个成员就是关掉它的位。询问就是检查一位。`,"Each is O(1), and all eight possible members fit in one byte.":`每个都是 O(1)，而且全部八个可能的成员都放得进一个字节。`,"add 6":`添加 6`,"A second set":`第二个集合`,"Behind is another set, B = {3, 4, 5}. Combining two sets usually means walking through the members of both.":`后面是另一个集合，B = {3, 4, 5}。合并两个集合通常意味着把两者的成员都走一遍。`,"Here each set is just a number, and the two rows line up bit for bit.":`这里每个集合都只是一个数，两排一位对一位地对齐。`,"Intersection is AND":`交集就是 AND`,Combine:`合并`,"Which members are in <em>both</em>? AND the two numbers. A bit survives only where both rows have a block.":`哪些成员在<em>两个</em>集合里？把两个数做 AND。只有两排都有方块的地方，那一位才会保留。`,"1 and 6 drop out, leaving {3, 4}. Every member was handled at once, by one instruction.":`1 和 6 掉出去了，剩下 {3, 4}。每个成员都同时处理了，用的是一条指令。`,"in both":`两个都有`,"Union is OR":`并集就是 OR`,"Put A back as it was. Which members are in <em>either</em> set? OR the two numbers: a bit is on if it is on in A or in B.":`把 A 恢复原样。哪些成员在<em>任意一个</em>集合里？把两个数做 OR：在 A 或 B 中开着的位就是开着的。`,"5 arrives from B, giving {1, 3, 4, 5, 6}. Taking B’s members <em>out</em> of A is A AND (NOT B).":`5 从 B 来，得到 {1, 3, 4, 5, 6}。把 B 的成员<em>从</em> A 中去掉就是 A AND (NOT B)。`,"When the members are small numbers":`当成员是小数字时`,"A real bitset is an array of 64-bit words. A set over a million possible members is about 16,000 words, and a union is 16,000 ORs.":`真正的位集合是一个由 64 位字组成的数组。一个有一百万个可能成员的集合大约是 16,000 个字，一次并集就是 16,000 次 OR。`,"It only works when members are small whole numbers, or can be numbered. A Bloom filter is built on one; so are the “visited” marks of a graph search and the sieve for finding primes.":`只有当成员是小的整数，或者能被编号时，它才管用。布隆过滤器就是建立在它上面的；图搜索中的“已访问”标记和找素数的筛法也是。`,"O(1) per member. O(n ÷ 64) to combine two whole sets of n possible members.":`每个成员 O(1)。合并两个有 n 个可能成员的完整集合要 O(n ÷ 64)。`},l={"binary-search":{"A sorted shelf":`排好序的架子`,"Nine numbers, in order from smallest to largest. We want to know where <strong>34</strong> is.":`九个数，从小到大排列。我们想知道 <strong>34</strong> 在哪里。`,"Checking every block from the left would get there in the end. Because the shelf is sorted, we can do far better.":`从左边逐个检查每个方块，最终也能找到。但因为架子是排好序的，我们可以做得好得多。`,"Binary search only works when the data is sorted.":`二分查找只适用于排好序的数据。`,"Look in the middle":`看中间`,"Mark the whole shelf as the search window, from <strong>low</strong> to <strong>high</strong>, and hold 34 up against the block in the middle.":`把整个架子标为搜索窗口，从 <strong>low</strong> 到 <strong>high</strong>，拿 34 和中间的方块比一比。`,"It is 28. That is less than 34.":`它是 28。比 34 小。`,"On a sorted shelf, everything to the left of 28 is smaller still. 34 cannot be there.":`在排好序的架子上，28 左边的一切都更小。34 不可能在那里。`,"Throw away half":`扔掉一半`,"28 and everything to its left is ruled out in one go. Move <strong>low</strong> to just past the middle.":`28 和它左边的一切一下子全被排除了。把 <strong>low</strong> 移到中间的后一位。`,"The window is now four blocks wide.":`窗口现在只有四个方块宽。`,"One look removed five candidates. Checking one by one, it would have removed one.":`看一次就排除了五个候选。逐个检查的话，只能排除一个。`,"Middle again":`再看中间`,"Do exactly the same thing on what is left. The middle of the window is now 42.":`对剩下的部分做完全相同的事。窗口的中间现在是 42。`,"That is more than 34, so 42 and everything to its right is too big.":`它比 34 大，所以 42 和它右边的一切都太大了。`,"That hop was half as long as the first. The next will be half as long again.":`这一跳是第一跳的一半长。下一跳又会是一半长。`,"And the other side":`再看另一边`,"Move <strong>high</strong> to just before the middle. Low and high now point at the same block.":`把 <strong>high</strong> 移到中间的前一位。low 和 high 现在指向同一个方块。`,"One candidate is left.":`只剩一个候选了。`,"Hold it up one last time: <strong>34 = 34</strong>. Found at index 5, after three looks.":`最后再比一次：<strong>34 = 34</strong>。在下标 5 找到，看了三次。`,"Had it been some other number, the window would have closed with nothing in it, and we would know 34 is not on the shelf.":`如果是别的数，窗口就会在里面什么都没有时合上，我们就知道 34 不在架子上。`,"Going one by one from the left would have taken six looks.":`从左边逐个看的话，要看六次。`,"Every look halves the window. So the number of looks depends on how many times you can halve n before one block is left: <strong>O(log n)</strong>.":`每看一次，窗口就减半。所以要看的次数取决于 n 能减半多少次才剩下一个方块：<strong>O(log n)</strong>。`,"Double the length of the shelf and the search needs just one more look.":`架子长度翻倍，搜索只需多看一次。`,"A million sorted items never take more than 20 looks.":`一百万个排好序的项，永远不会超过 20 次。`},"binary-search-on-answer":{"while lo < hi:":`当 lo < hi:`,"mid ← halfway between lo and hi":`mid ← lo 和 hi 的中点`,"if works(mid):":`如果 works(mid):`,"hi ← mid          // mid may be the answer":`hi ← mid          // mid 可能就是答案`,"lo ← mid + 1      // mid is too small":`lo ← mid + 1      // mid 太小了`,"return lo":`返回 lo`,"load the parcels in order, starting a new":`按顺序装包裹，下一个装不下时`,"trip when the next one will not fit":`就开始新的一趟`,"return trips used ≤ trips allowed":`返回 用掉的趟数 ≤ 允许的趟数`,"No array to search":`没有数组可搜`,"Three parcels weighing 5, 3 and 4 must go out in order, in at most two trips. What is the <strong>smallest lorry</strong> that can do it?":`重 5、3、4 的三个包裹必须按顺序送出，最多送两趟。能做到的<strong>最小卡车</strong>是多大？`,"It must hold the biggest parcel, so at least 5. A lorry of 12 takes everything at once. The answer is somewhere in the row 5 to 12, and nothing in the problem is sorted.":`它必须装得下最大的包裹，所以至少是 5。容量 12 的卡车一次就能装下全部。答案在 5 到 12 这一排里的某处，而问题里没有任何东西是排好序的。`,Parcels:`包裹`,"in this order":`按这个顺序`,"Trips allowed":`允许的趟数`,"Could still be":`仍有可能`,"5 to 12":`5 到 12`,"Sizes tested":`已测试的容量`,"Guess the middle and check":`猜中间，然后检查`,"Finding the best size directly is awkward. <em>Checking</em> one size is easy: load parcels until the next will not fit, then start a new trip.":`直接找出最佳容量很麻烦。<em>检查</em>一个容量却很容易：装包裹，直到下一个装不下，然后开始新的一趟。`,"Try 8. First trip 5 + 3, second trip 4. Two trips: it works. So anything bigger works too, and hi comes down to 8.":`试试 8。第一趟 5 + 3，第二趟 4。两趟：可行。所以更大的也都可行，hi 降到 8。`,"5+3, then 4":`5+3，然后 4`,"5 to 8":`5 到 8`,"Too small":`太小`,"Middle of 5 to 8: try 6. Trip one takes 5, trip two takes 3, and 4 is left over. Three trips: it fails.":`5 到 8 的中间：试试 6。第一趟装 5，第二趟装 3，4 剩下了。三趟：不行。`,"So anything smaller fails too. lo moves past it, to 7.":`所以更小的也都不行。lo 越过它，移到 7。`,"5, 3, 4: three trips":`5、3、4：三趟`,"7 to 8":`7 到 8`,"Closing in":`逼近`,"Try 7. Trip one takes 5, trip two takes 3 + 4. It works, so hi comes down to 7.":`试试 7。第一趟装 5，第二趟装 3 + 4。可行，所以 hi 降到 7。`,"lo and hi now meet. The smallest lorry is 7, found with three checks.":`lo 和 hi 现在相遇了。最小的卡车是 7，检查了三次就找到了。`,"5, then 3+4":`5，然后 3+4`,"The sorted row was hidden":`排好序的一排藏起来了`,"Why it works":`为什么可行`,"Write down the answer to “does this size work?” for every size, and the row reads no, no, yes, yes, yes… All the noes come first, then all the yeses.":`把每个容量对“这个容量可行吗？”的回答写下来，这一排读起来就是否、否、是、是、是……所有的“否”在前，然后全是“是”。`,"That is a sorted row. Binary search needs nothing more: it is looking for the place where no turns into yes.":`这就是一排排好序的东西。二分查找不需要别的：它要找的就是“否”变成“是”的那个位置。`,"Never worked out: 5, 9, 10, 11, 12.":`从没算过：5、9、10、11、12。`,"Smallest that works":`最小的可行值`,"Look for this shape: “the smallest X such that…” or “the largest X such that…”, where a check is easy and making X bigger can only help.":`留意这种形式：“满足……的最小 X”或者“满足……的最大 X”，其中检查很容易，而且让 X 变大只会有帮助。`,"The slowest speed that still arrives on time. The largest gap you can keep between items. The smallest page size that fits a book into k volumes.":`仍能准时到达的最慢速度。物品之间能保持的最大间距。能把一本书装进 k 卷的最小页面大小。`,"O(n) per check, and log(range) checks: O(n log range) in all.":`每次检查 O(n)，检查 log(范围) 次：总共 O(n log 范围)。`},"simple-sorts":{"find the smallest item from i onwards":`找出从 i 开始往后最小的项`,"swap it into cell i":`把它交换到格子 i`,"for each item, from the second onwards:":`对每个 项，从第二个开始:`,"lift it out":`把它拿出来`,"shift every bigger item before it one cell right":`把它前面每个更大的项右移一格`,"put it down in the gap":`把它放进空出来的位置`,"Put them in order":`把它们排好序`,"Six numbers, in no order. Sorting is one of the oldest problems in computing, and a sorted array is what makes binary search possible.":`六个数，没有顺序。排序是计算机领域最古老的问题之一，而排好序的数组正是二分查找的前提。`,"The simple sorts all work the same way: grow a sorted part at one end, one item at a time. They are easy to write and easy to trust.":`简单排序的原理都一样：在一端扩展一个已排序的部分，一次一项。它们容易写，也容易让人放心。`,Method:`方法`,"In order so far":`目前已就位`,"Selection: find the smallest":`选择：找出最小的`,"Selection sort":`选择排序`,"Look at every item and remember the smallest seen so far: 5, then 2, then 1. Swap it into the first cell.":`看每一项，记住目前见过最小的：5，然后 2，然后 1。把它交换到第一个格子。`,"Cell 0 now holds the right value for good. It is never looked at again.":`格子 0 现在永久存着正确的值。再也不会看它了。`,"Then the next smallest":`然后是第二小的`,"Do the same with what is left. The smallest of the rest is 2, already in place. After it comes 3, which swaps with 8.":`对剩下的做同样的事。其余中最小的是 2，已经就位了。之后是 3，它和 8 交换。`,"Each pass scans everything that is not yet sorted, and fixes exactly one more cell.":`每一趟都扫描所有还没排好的项，并且恰好多确定一个格子。`,"2: already in place":`2：已经就位`,"Until nothing is left":`直到什么都不剩`,"Two more swaps and the row is sorted.":`再交换两次，这一排就排好了。`,"Six items took six passes, and each pass looked at everything unsorted: 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 comparisons. Double the items and that is four times the work.":`六个项用了六趟，每趟都要看所有没排好的：5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 次比较。项数翻倍，工作量就变成四倍。`,"O(n²) comparisons, always. At most n swaps, which is the one thing it is good at.":`比较次数总是 O(n²)。交换最多 n 次，这是它唯一擅长的地方。`,"15 comparisons for 6 items.":`6 个项比较 15 次。`,"Insertion: a sorted part":`插入：一个已排序的部分`,"Insertion sort":`插入排序`,"Start again with the same six, and a different idea. Treat the first item as a sorted list of one.":`用同样的六个数重新开始，换一个思路。把第一项当作只有一项的有序列表。`,"Then take the items one at a time and slot each into its place in that list. It is how most people sort a hand of cards.":`然后一次取一项，把每一项插到那个列表中它该在的位置。大多数人整理手里的扑克牌就是这样做的。`,"sorted, so far":`目前已排序`,"Lift, shift, drop":`拿起、挪动、放下`,"Take 2. It is smaller than 5, so lift it out, slide 5 one cell to the right, and put 2 down in the gap.":`取 2。它比 5 小，所以把它拿出来，把 5 右移一格，再把 2 放进空位。`,"The sorted part is now two long.":`已排序的部分现在有两项长。`,"Only as far as needed":`只走需要走的距离`,"8 is already bigger than everything before it: one comparison, no moves. 3 has to go back past 8 and 5, and stops when it meets 2.":`8 已经比它前面的一切都大：一次比较，不用移动。3 要退过 8 和 5，遇到 2 时停下。`,"An item only travels as far as it is out of place.":`一项只会移动它偏离位置的那么远。`,"8 > 5: stays":`8 > 5：不动`,"Simple, and sometimes right":`简单，有时正合适`,"1 travels all the way to the front; 6 moves back one place. Sorted.":`1 一路走到最前面；6 往回挪一位。排好了。`,"In the worst case insertion sort is O(n²) too. But on data that is already nearly sorted it does almost nothing, close to O(n), which is why real sorting libraries use it for small or nearly sorted pieces.":`最坏情况下插入排序也是 O(n²)。但在已经差不多排好的数据上，它几乎什么都不用做，接近 O(n)，所以真正的排序库会用它来处理小的或几乎有序的片段。`,Also:`另外`,"Bubble sort, which swaps neighbours that are out of order, is the third simple sort. It is O(n²) and rarely the best choice.":`冒泡排序交换顺序不对的相邻项，是第三种简单排序。它是 O(n²)，很少是最好的选择。`},"merge-sort":{"if a has fewer than two items: return a":`如果 a 少于两项: 返回 a`,"left ← merge_sort(the first half)":`left ← merge_sort(前一半)`,"right ← merge_sort(the second half)":`right ← merge_sort(后一半)`,"return merge(left, right)":`返回 merge(left, right)`,"while both have items:":`当 两边都还有项:`,"move the smaller of their front items to the output":`把两边队首中较小的移到输出`,"move whatever is left over to the output":`把剩下的全部移到输出`,"Divide and conquer":`分治`,"The simple sorts take about n² steps. <strong>Merge sort</strong> does much better, with an idea borrowed from recursion: a big sorting problem is two smaller sorting problems.":`简单排序大约要 n² 步。<strong>归并排序</strong>做得好得多，它借用了递归的思路：一个大的排序问题就是两个小的排序问题。`,"Sort the left half. Sort the right half. Then combine two sorted halves into one, which turns out to be easy.":`排好左半边。排好右半边。然后把两个排好的半边合成一个，而这件事其实很容易。`,"Moved to the output":`已移到输出`,"Levels of halving":`对半分的层数`,"Moves per level":`每层移动次数`,"Split in half":`对半分`,"Cut the row down the middle. Nothing is compared and nothing moves: the split is just two index ranges.":`从中间切开这一排。不做比较，也不移动任何东西：切分只是两个下标范围。`,"Each half is a smaller copy of the original problem.":`每一半都是原问题的一个更小的副本。`,"Sort each half the same way":`用同样的方法排好每一半`,"Each half is sorted by merge sort itself: split again, and again, until the pieces are one item long. A single item is already sorted. That is the base case.":`每一半都由归并排序自己来排：再切，再切，直到每块只有一项长。单独一项本来就是有序的。这就是基本情况。`,"Trust the recursion for now. What comes back is two sorted halves: 2 3 5 8 and 1 4 6 7.":`现在先相信递归。返回来的是两个排好的半边：2 3 5 8 和 1 4 6 7。`,"Each half is in order. The whole row is not.":`每一半都是有序的。整排还不是。`,"Merge: compare the fronts":`合并：比较队首`,Merge:`合并`,"Now the real work. The smallest item overall must be at the front of one half or the other, so compare just those two: 1 beats 2. Move it to the output.":`现在是真正的工作。所有项中最小的一定在某一半的最前面，所以只比较这两个：1 胜过 2。把它移到输出。`,"Again: 2 against 4. Each move takes one comparison.":`再来：2 对 4。每次移动只要一次比较。`,"Keep taking the smaller":`一直取较小的`,"3, then 4, then 5, 6 and 7. Every time, only the two front items are looked at, because each half is already in order.":`3，然后 4，然后 5、6 和 7。每次只看两个队首的项，因为每一半都已经有序。`,"The second half has run out.":`后一半用完了。`,"With one half empty, whatever is left in the other goes straight across. Eight items merged with eight moves.":`一半空了之后，另一半剩下的直接移过去。八个项，八次移动就合并好了。`,"Every level of splitting needs one such pass over all n items, and halving 8 down to 1 takes 3 levels: log₂ n of them. So the whole sort is n × log n, on any input.":`每一层切分都需要对全部 n 个项过一遍，而把 8 对半分到 1 要 3 层：log₂ n 层。所以整个排序是 n × log n，对任何输入都是。`,"O(n log n) always. The price is the second row: O(n) extra space.":`总是 O(n log n)。代价是第二排：O(n) 额外空间。`,"For a million items: 20 levels, not a million passes.":`一百万个项：20 层，而不是一百万趟。`},"quick-sort":{"if a has fewer than two items: return":`如果 a 少于两项: 返回`,"quick_sort(everything before p)":`quick_sort(p 之前的一切)`,"quick_sort(everything after p)":`quick_sort(p 之后的一切)`,"pivot ← the last item":`pivot ← 最后一项`,"i ← the first cell":`i ← 第一个格子`,"for each item before the pivot, at j:":`对每个 基准之前的项，位置为 j:`,"if it is smaller than the pivot:":`如果 它比基准小:`,"swap it into cell i, and move i along":`把它交换到格子 i，然后 i 前移`,"swap the pivot into cell i":`把基准交换到格子 i`,"return i":`返回 i`,"Around the pivot":`围绕基准`,"Pick a pivot":`选一个基准`,"Merge sort splits blindly and does its work when combining. <strong>Quick sort</strong> does the work first: it splits <em>by value</em>, so that no combining is needed.":`归并排序盲目地切分，在合并时才干活。<strong>快速排序</strong>先干活：它<em>按值</em>切分，这样就不需要合并了。`,"Choose one item as the <strong>pivot</strong>, here the last, 4. The aim is to get everything smaller to its left and everything bigger to its right.":`选一项作为<strong>基准</strong>，这里选最后一项 4。目标是让所有更小的都在它左边，所有更大的都在它右边。`,"the pivot":`基准`,Pivot:`基准`,"Smaller, on its left":`更小的，在它左边`,"Bigger, on its right":`更大的，在它右边`,"Smaller ones go left":`小的去左边`,Partition:`划分`,"Scan along with j. Cell i marks where the next small item should go. 5 is bigger than the pivot: leave it. 2 is smaller: swap it into cell i, and move i along.":`用 j 往后扫。格子 i 标记下一个小项该放的位置。5 比基准大：不动。2 更小：把它交换到格子 i，然后 i 前移。`,"5 > 4: leave it":`5 > 4：不动`,"2 < 4: goes left":`2 < 4：去左边`,"Keep scanning":`继续扫描`,"8 stays. 3 is small: swap it into cell i. 7 stays. 1 is small: swap. 6 stays.":`8 不动。3 小：把它交换到格子 i。7 不动。1 小：交换。6 不动。`,"Everything before i is now smaller than the pivot, and everything from i up to the pivot is bigger. Neither side is sorted, and that is fine.":`现在 i 之前的一切都比基准小，从 i 到基准之间的一切都更大。两边都没排序，这没关系。`,"The pivot drops into place":`基准落到位`,"Finally swap the pivot into cell i, between the two groups.":`最后把基准交换到格子 i，放在两组之间。`,"4 is now exactly where it will be in the sorted row: three smaller items before it, four bigger after. It never moves again.":`4 现在正好在它在有序排列中的位置：前面三个更小的项，后面四个更大的。它再也不会移动了。`,"The same again, each side":`两边各做一遍同样的事`,"Now sort the left group and the right group in the same way: pick a pivot, partition, repeat. Each partition puts one more item in its final place and leaves two smaller problems.":`现在用同样的方法排左边一组和右边一组：选基准、划分、重复。每次划分都让多一个项到达最终位置，并留下两个更小的问题。`,"When the pieces are down to one item, the whole row is sorted. Nothing has to be merged.":`当每块只剩一项时，整排就排好了。不需要合并任何东西。`,"Fast, usually":`通常很快`,"When the pivot lands near the middle, the row halves each time: log n levels of n work, like merge sort, but in place and with less copying. In practice it is often the fastest sort there is.":`当基准落在中间附近时，这一排每次都会减半：log n 层，每层 n 的工作，和归并排序一样，但它是原地进行的，复制也更少。实践中它往往是最快的排序。`,"When the pivot is always the smallest or biggest, one side is empty and nothing halves. On a row that is already sorted, “pick the last item” does exactly that.":`如果基准总是最小或最大的，一边就是空的，什么都没减半。在已经排好序的一排上，“选最后一项”恰好就会这样。`,"O(n log n) on average, O(n²) at worst. Picking the pivot at random makes the worst case vanishingly unlikely.":`平均 O(n log n)，最坏 O(n²)。随机选基准能让最坏情况几乎不可能出现。`,"sorted in place":`原地排好`,"No second row was needed.":`不需要第二排。`},quickselect:e,"counting-radix-sort":{"for each item x in a:":`对每个 a 中的项 x:`,"put x in bucket x":`把 x 放进 x 号桶`,"read the buckets back in order":`按顺序把桶里的东西读回来`,"for each digit, from the last to the first:":`对每个 数位，从最后一位到第一位:`,"put each item in the bucket for that digit,":`把每一项放进对应这个数位的桶，`,"keeping the order they arrive in":`保持它们到达的顺序`,"Sorting without comparing":`不用比较的排序`,"Every sort so far works by comparing two items, and no such sort can beat n log n. But comparing is not the only way.":`到目前为止的每种排序都是靠比较两项来工作的，而这样的排序都不可能快过 n log n。但比较并不是唯一的方法。`,"If the items are small whole numbers, a number can be used as an <em>address</em>. Behind the row is a bucket for each possible value, 0 to 5.":`如果这些项是小的整数，数字本身就可以当作<em>地址</em>用。这一排后面，每个可能的值都有一个桶，从 0 到 5。`,Comparisons:`比较次数`,Moves:`移动次数`,"Each to its own bucket":`各进各的桶`,"Counting sort":`计数排序`,"Take the items in order and drop each into the bucket with its number. 3 goes to bucket 3, 1 to bucket 1.":`按顺序取出每一项，把它丢进和它数字相同的桶。3 进 3 号桶，1 进 1 号桶。`,"No item is ever compared with another. Each one knows where it belongs.":`没有任何一项和别的项比较过。每一项都知道自己该去哪里。`,"Read the buckets back":`把桶读回来`,"Now empty the buckets from left to right. The values come out in order, because the buckets <em>are</em> in order.":`现在从左到右清空各个桶。值按顺序出来了，因为这些桶<em>本身</em>就是有序的。`,"Two passes, and the work depends on the number of items plus the number of buckets, not on n log n.":`两趟，而工作量取决于项数加上桶数，而不是 n log n。`,"O(n + k) for n items and k possible values. Only sensible when k is small.":`n 个项、k 种可能的值时为 O(n + k)。只有 k 很小时才合理。`,"Bigger numbers":`更大的数`,"Radix sort":`基数排序`,"These numbers go up to 51. One bucket per possible value would mean dozens of buckets, mostly empty, and for bigger numbers, millions.":`这些数最大到 51。每个可能的值一个桶，就意味着要几十个桶，大部分是空的；数再大一些，就要几百万个。`,"<strong>Radix sort</strong> keeps the six buckets and sorts by one digit at a time instead.":`<strong>基数排序</strong>保留这六个桶，改为一次按一个数位排序。`,"By the last digit":`按最后一位`,"First pass: ignore the tens and bucket each number by its <em>last</em> digit. 32 goes to bucket 2, 15 to bucket 5.":`第一趟：忽略十位，按每个数的<em>最后一位</em>放进桶里。32 进 2 号桶，15 进 5 号桶。`,"Where two share a bucket, the one that arrived first stays in front: 32 ahead of 12.":`两个数在同一个桶里时，先到的留在前面：32 在 12 前面。`,"Read them back":`读回来`,"Empty the buckets in order, front of each bucket first. The row is now sorted by last digit: 1, 2, 2, 3, 5, 5.":`按顺序清空各个桶，每个桶先取前面的。这一排现在按最后一位排好了：1、2、2、3、5、5。`,"It does not look sorted yet. One more pass.":`看起来还没排好。再来一趟。`,"Then by the first digit":`然后按第一位`,"Second pass: bucket by the tens digit. 12 and 15 both go to bucket 1, and 12 arrives first because the last pass put it first.":`第二趟：按十位放进桶里。12 和 15 都进 1 号桶，12 先到，因为上一趟把它排在了前面。`,"That is the trick. Keeping arrival order means the work of the earlier pass is not undone.":`诀窍就在这里。保持到达顺序，意味着前一趟的工作不会被打乱。`,"The word for it":`这个性质的名字`,"A sort that keeps equal items in their original order is called stable. Radix sort depends on it.":`让相等的项保持原来顺序的排序叫作稳定排序。基数排序依赖于它。`,"Sorted, digit by digit":`一位一位地排好`,"Read the buckets back once more: 12, 15, 23, 32, 35, 51. Sorted, with not one comparison between two numbers.":`再把桶读回来一次：12、15、23、32、35、51。排好了，两个数之间一次比较都没有。`,"Each pass is a counting sort on one digit, so the total is the number of digits times the size of the input.":`每一趟都是对一个数位的计数排序，所以总量是数位个数乘以输入的大小。`,"O(d × (n + k)) for d digits. Excellent for fixed-size keys such as integers, dates and postcodes.":`d 个数位时为 O(d × (n + k))。非常适合固定长度的键，比如整数、日期和邮政编码。`,"Two digits: two passes.":`两个数位：两趟。`},"stability-and-limits":{"When two keys are equal":`当两个键相等时`,"Two of these cards carry a 3. They are different cards, 3a and 3b, and 3a came first.":`这些卡片中有两张是 3。它们是不同的卡片，3a 和 3b，而 3a 在前。`,"A sort only cares about the number. So after sorting, which 3 should be in front? There are two honest answers, and sorts differ in which one they give.":`排序只关心数字。那么排序之后，哪个 3 应该在前面？有两个说得通的答案，而不同的排序给出的答案不同。`,"3a came first":`3a 在前`,"Sorted with":`使用的排序`,"The two 3s":`两个 3`,"3a, then 3b":`3a，然后 3b`,Stable:`稳定`,merge:`归并`,counting:`计数`,radix:`基数`,"Not stable":`不稳定`,quick:`快速`,heap:`堆`,"A long swap jumps the queue":`一次远距离交换插了队`,Unstable:`不稳定`,"Selection sort: find the smallest and swap it to the front. 1 swaps with 3a. Then the next smallest, 2, swaps with 3a again.":`选择排序：找出最小的，把它交换到最前面。1 和 3a 交换。然后第二小的 2 又和 3a 交换。`,"That second swap carried 3a right over 3b. The row is sorted, but the two 3s have changed places. A sort that can do this is <strong>unstable</strong>.":`第二次交换把 3a 直接带过了 3b。这一排排好了，但两个 3 换了位置。会这样做的排序是<strong>不稳定</strong>的。`,"smallest: 1":`最小：1`,"next smallest: 2":`第二小：2`,"3b is now in front":`3b 现在在前面`,"selection sort":`选择排序`,swapped:`已交换`,"Why anyone minds":`为什么有人在意`,Why:`为什么`,"Deal the same four again. Suppose the letter is a name and the number a grade, and the list arrives in name order. Sort it by grade with an unstable sort and the names inside each grade come out shuffled.":`再发同样的四张。假设字母是名字，数字是成绩，列表按名字顺序到来。用不稳定的排序按成绩排，每个成绩里的名字就会被打乱。`,"A <strong>stable</strong> sort keeps equal keys in the order they arrived. That is what makes “sort by name, then by grade” work.":`<strong>稳定</strong>的排序让相等的键保持它们到达的顺序。正是这一点让“先按名字排，再按成绩排”行得通。`,"Insertion never passes an equal":`插入排序从不越过相等的项`,"Insertion sort lifts each card and slides the <em>bigger</em> ones along to make room. 1 goes in front of 3a. 3b is not smaller than 3a, so it stays put.":`插入排序拿起每张卡片，把<em>更大</em>的往后挪来腾出位置。1 放到 3a 前面。3b 不比 3a 小，所以它不动。`,"2 slides in under both 3s, which each move one place and keep their order. Nothing ever hops over a card equal to it.":`2 滑到两个 3 的前面，两个 3 各挪一位，保持它们的顺序。从来没有卡片越过和它相等的卡片。`,"3b: not smaller, stays":`3b：不更小，不动`,"still 3a, then 3b":`仍是 3a，然后 3b`,"insertion sort":`插入排序`,"Which sorts are which":`哪些排序是哪种`,Summary:`总结`,"Sorts that only move cards past strictly bigger neighbours, or that merge taking from the left side first, are stable: insertion, merge, counting and radix.":`只让卡片越过严格更大的邻居的排序，或者合并时先从左边取的排序，是稳定的：插入、归并、计数和基数。`,"Sorts that swap across a distance are not: selection, quick sort and heap sort. Any of them can be made stable by sorting on the pair (key, original position), at the cost of extra memory.":`远距离交换的排序不是：选择排序、快速排序和堆排序。它们都可以通过按 (键, 原始位置) 这一对来排序而变得稳定，代价是额外的内存。`,"Radix sort relies on it: each pass must not undo the last.":`基数排序依赖于它：每一趟都不能打乱上一趟。`,"How fast can sorting be?":`排序最快能有多快？`,"A different question about the same cards. A sort that works by comparing learns one thing per comparison: yes or no. Four cards can arrive in 24 different orders, and the sort has to find out which.":`关于同样这些卡片的另一个问题。靠比较工作的排序，每次比较只能得知一件事：是或否。四张卡片可能有 24 种不同的到达顺序，而排序必须找出是哪一种。`,"A yes-or-no answer can at best rule out half of the orders still possible. 24, 12, 6, 3, 2, 1: no method can be sure in fewer than five comparisons.":`一个是或否的回答，最多只能排除仍然可能的顺序中的一半。24、12、6、3、2、1：没有任何方法能用少于五次比较就确定。`,"one of 24 orders":`24 种顺序之一`,"Possible orders of 4 cards":`4 张卡片可能的顺序`,"Left after each answer":`每次回答后剩下的`,"at best":`最好情况`,"Comparisons needed":`需要的比较次数`,"at least":`至少`,"For n items":`n 个项时`,"about n log n":`大约 n log n`,"n log n is the floor":`n log n 是下限`,"For n items there are n! orders, and halving that down to one takes about n log n answers. So every comparison sort needs that many in its worst case. Merge sort and heap sort already achieve it: they cannot be beaten, only matched.":`n 个项有 n! 种顺序，把它减半到只剩一种大约需要 n log n 个回答。所以每种比较排序在最坏情况下都需要这么多次。归并排序和堆排序已经做到了：它们不可能被超越，只能被追平。`,"Counting and radix sort go faster only because they never compare. They read the keys directly, which is a different game with its own conditions.":`计数排序和基数排序之所以更快，只是因为它们从不比较。它们直接读取键，这是另一种玩法，有它自己的条件。`,"The limit":`极限`,"No comparison sort can do better than O(n log n) in the worst case.":`在最坏情况下，没有比较排序能好过 O(n log n)。`,"Proved, not just observed.":`是证明出来的，不只是观察到的。`},"interval-scheduling":{"sort them by when they finish":`按结束时间排序`,"free_from ← the start of the day":`free_from ← 一天的开始`,"for each request, in that order:":`对每个 请求，按那个顺序:`,"if it starts at or after free_from:":`如果 它在 free_from 或之后开始:`,"take it":`接受它`,"free_from ← when it finishes":`free_from ← 它结束的时间`,"The room":`会议室`,"One room, five requests":`一间会议室，五个请求`,"Five meetings want the same room. Each row is one request, and each block is an hour it needs. Two meetings cannot overlap.":`五个会议想用同一间会议室。每一行是一个请求，每个方块是它需要的一个小时。两个会议不能重叠。`,"Which ones should be accepted to fit in <strong>as many meetings as possible</strong>?":`应该接受哪些，才能安排<strong>尽可能多的会议</strong>？`,Taken:`已接受`,"Turned down":`已拒绝`,"Room free from":`会议室空出的时间`,"hour 0":`第 0 小时`,"A rule that sounds right":`听起来对的规则`,"Wrong turn":`走错路`,"A <strong>greedy</strong> algorithm makes one simple choice after another and never takes one back. The whole question is which rule to choose by.":`<strong>贪心</strong>算法一个接一个地做简单的选择，并且从不反悔。整个问题就在于按什么规则来选。`,"Try “whichever starts first”. That is D, and D holds the room for six hours. Every other request overlaps it: one meeting.":`试试“最先开始的”。那是 D，而 D 占用会议室六个小时。其他每个请求都和它重叠：一个会议。`,"starts first, blocks four":`最先开始，挡住了四个`,"hour 6":`第 6 小时`,"Whichever finishes first":`最先结束的`,"The rule that works: take the meeting that <strong>finishes earliest</strong>. It hands the room back soonest, leaving the most time for everything else.":`行得通的规则是：选<strong>最早结束</strong>的会议。它最快把会议室交还出来，给其他一切留下最多的时间。`,"The rows are already in that order. A finishes first, at hour 3. Take it.":`各行已经按这个顺序排好了。A 最先结束，在第 3 小时。接受它。`,"finishes first":`最先结束`,"hour 3":`第 3 小时`,"Skip what overlaps":`跳过重叠的`,"Go down the list. B starts at hour 2, while A still has the room. Turn it down.":`沿着列表往下走。B 在第 2 小时开始，这时 A 还占着会议室。拒绝它。`,"C starts at hour 3, exactly as A leaves. Take it. The room is now busy until hour 5.":`C 在第 3 小时开始，正好是 A 离开的时候。接受它。会议室现在一直忙到第 5 小时。`,"starts as A ends":`在 A 结束时开始`,"hour 5":`第 5 小时`,"One pass to the end":`一趟到底`,"D started back at hour 0: turned down. E starts at hour 5, as C leaves: taken.":`D 早在第 0 小时就开始了：拒绝。E 在第 5 小时开始，正好 C 离开：接受。`,"Three meetings, A, C and E, and each request was looked at once.":`三个会议，A、C 和 E，每个请求只看了一次。`,"starts as C ends":`在 C 结束时开始`,"hour 8":`第 8 小时`,"Why it cannot be beaten":`为什么无法被超越`,"Take any best possible schedule and look at its first meeting. Swap it for A. A finishes no later, so nothing after it is disturbed, and the schedule is just as long.":`取任意一个最佳安排，看它的第一个会议。把它换成 A。A 不会结束得更晚，所以它后面的一切都不受影响，安排也一样长。`,"So there is always a best schedule that starts with the greedy choice. The same argument then applies to whatever comes after A.":`所以总存在一个以贪心选择开头的最佳安排。同样的论证也适用于 A 之后的一切。`,"O(n log n) to sort, then one pass.":`排序 O(n log n)，然后一趟。`,"No schedule fits in four.":`没有任何安排能放下四个。`},"huffman-coding":{"put every letter in a min-heap, by count":`把每个字母按次数放进一个最小堆`,"while the heap holds more than one node:":`当 堆中不止一个节点:`,"a ← pop the smallest":`a ← 弹出最小的`,"b ← pop the smallest":`b ← 弹出最小的`,"push a new node worth a + b,":`压入一个值为 a + b 的新节点，`,"with a and b as its children":`以 a 和 b 作为它的孩子`,"return the last node          // the root":`返回 最后一个节点          // 根`,"walk from the root down to the letter:":`从根往下走到这个字母:`,"going left adds a 0, going right a 1":`往左加一个 0，往右加一个 1`,"The codes":`编码`,"Short codes for common letters":`常用字母用短编码`,"A message of 13 letters uses only four: A eight times, B three times, C and D once each. Giving every letter a 2-bit code takes 26 bits.":`一条 13 个字母的消息只用到四个字母：A 八次，B 三次，C 和 D 各一次。给每个字母一个 2 位编码，需要 26 位。`,"It would be shorter if A, which is most of the message, had a 1-bit code. The price is longer codes for the rare letters. <strong>Huffman coding</strong> finds the best trade.":`如果占了消息大部分的 A 有一个 1 位编码，就会更短。代价是罕见字母的编码更长。<strong>哈夫曼编码</strong>能找到最好的取舍。`,"appears 8×":`出现 8 次`,"appears 3×":`出现 3 次`,"appears 1×":`出现 1 次`,"Bits for the message":`消息所需的位数`,"Two bits each.":`每个两位。`,"Join the two rarest":`合并最罕见的两个`,"Find the two smallest counts: C and D, 1 each. Hang them from a new node worth their sum, 2.":`找出最小的两个次数：C 和 D，各 1 次。把它们挂在一个新节点下，新节点的值是它们的和 2。`,"From now on that pair is treated as a single item that appears twice.":`从现在起，这一对被当作一个出现两次的项。`,"Three items are left: A at 8, B at 3 and the pair at 2. The two smallest are B and the pair. Join them under a node worth 5.":`剩下三个项：A 为 8，B 为 3，这一对为 2。最小的两个是 B 和这一对。把它们合并到一个值为 5 的节点下。`,"C and D have just sunk a level deeper. Every time something is joined, everything under it gets one bit longer.":`C 和 D 刚刚又沉下去一层。每次有东西被合并，它下面的一切都会多一位。`,"Until one tree is left":`直到只剩一棵树`,"Two items left, A at 8 and the node at 5. Join them: 13, the length of the whole message. That node is the root.":`剩下两个项，A 为 8，节点为 5。合并它们：13，正是整条消息的长度。这个节点就是根。`,"A was never one of the two smallest, so it was joined last and sits right under the root.":`A 从来不是最小的两个之一，所以它最后才被合并，就在根的正下方。`,"Read the codes off the branches":`从树枝上读出编码`,"Going left is a 0 and going right is a 1. A letter’s code is the path to it from the root.":`往左是 0，往右是 1。一个字母的编码就是从根到它的路径。`,"A is 0. B is 10. C is 110 and D is 111. The message takes 8 × 1 + 3 × 2 + 1 × 3 + 1 × 3 = 20 bits, down from 26.":`A 是 0。B 是 10。C 是 110，D 是 111。消息需要 8 × 1 + 3 × 2 + 1 × 3 + 1 × 3 = 20 位，比 26 位少。`,"Six bits saved on thirteen letters.":`十三个字母省了六位。`,"No commas needed":`不需要分隔符`,Decoding:`解码`,"Letters only ever sit at the ends of branches, so no code is the beginning of another. To decode, start at the root and follow the bits until you land on a letter: 1, 1, 0 is C. Then start again at the root.":`字母只会出现在树枝的末端，所以没有一个编码是另一个编码的开头。解码时，从根开始沿着位走，直到落在一个字母上：1、1、0 是 C。然后再从根开始。`,"Always joining the two rarest is a greedy rule, and here greedy is provably the best possible.":`总是合并最罕见的两个是一个贪心规则，而在这里，贪心被证明是最好的。`,"O(n log n) with a min-heap. It is the last stage of ZIP, JPEG and MP3.":`用最小堆是 O(n log n)。它是 ZIP、JPEG 和 MP3 的最后一个阶段。`},"when-greedy-fails":{"while node has children:":`当 node 有孩子:`,"node ← the child with the bigger value":`node ← 值较大的那个孩子`,"return total":`返回 total`,"if node is nothing: return 0":`如果 node 为空: 返回 0`,"return node.value + the larger of":`返回 node.value + 以下两者中较大的`,"best_walk(node.left) and best_walk(node.right)":`best_walk(node.left) 和 best_walk(node.right)`,"Two walks":`两种走法`,"Take the best on offer":`拿眼前最好的`,"Every greedy algorithm has the same shape: at each step take whatever looks best right now, and never go back on it. That is what makes them fast, and simple to write.":`每个贪心算法都是同一个样子：每一步都拿现在看起来最好的东西，并且从不反悔。这正是它们快、而且写起来简单的原因。`,"Here is a test for the idea. Walk from the top node to the bottom, adding up the numbers you pass. The biggest total wins.":`这里有一个检验这个思路的例子。从最上面的节点走到最底下，把经过的数加起来。总和最大的赢。`,"start with 5":`从 5 开始`,"Greedy path":`贪心路径`,"Greedy total":`贪心总和`,"Best path":`最佳路径`,"not looked for":`没有去找`,"Best total":`最佳总和`,"The bigger number":`较大的数`,"Below the top are 7 and 3. Greedy does not hesitate: 7 is bigger. The total is 12.":`最上面的下方是 7 和 3。贪心毫不犹豫：7 更大。总和是 12。`,"The whole right-hand side of the tree has just been given up, without a look at what is in it.":`整棵树的右半边就这样被放弃了，连看都没看里面有什么。`,"7 beats 3":`7 胜过 3`,"Stuck with what is left":`只能接受剩下的`,"Under 7 the choice is between 1 and 2. Greedy takes 2 and finishes with 14.":`在 7 下面，要在 1 和 2 之间选。贪心选 2，最后得到 14。`,"Every single choice was the best one available at the time.":`每一个选择在当时都是可选的最好的一个。`,"total 14":`总和 14`,"What it never saw":`它从没看到的东西`,Counterexample:`反例`,"Go right at the top instead. 3 looks like the worse choice, but it leads to 9: a total of 17.":`在最上面改为往右走。3 看起来是更差的选择，但它通向 9：总和 17。`,"Greedy missed it because the 9 was hidden behind a small number. One good-looking choice at the start closed off the best answer for good.":`贪心错过了它，因为 9 藏在一个小数后面。开头一个看起来不错的选择，永远关上了通往最佳答案的门。`,"total 17":`总和 17`,"Looking at everything":`把一切都看一遍`,"To be sure of the best, every path has to be accounted for. Work upwards: the best total from each node is its own number plus the better of its two children’s totals.":`要确定得到最好的，每条路径都必须考虑到。从下往上做：每个节点出发的最佳总和，是它自己的数加上它两个孩子的总和中较好的那个。`,"From 7 the best is 9. From 3 it is 12. So from the top it is 5 + 12 = 17. That is dynamic programming, and it looks at every node once.":`从 7 出发最好是 9。从 3 出发是 12。所以从最上面出发是 5 + 12 = 17。这就是动态规划，每个节点只看一次。`,"When greedy is right":`贪心什么时候是对的`,"Greedy is only safe when you can argue that the best-looking choice is always part of <em>some</em> best answer. Earliest finish in interval scheduling passes that test. So do Huffman’s two rarest, and Kruskal’s cheapest edge.":`只有当你能论证看起来最好的选择总是<em>某个</em>最佳答案的一部分时，贪心才是安全的。区间调度中的最早结束通过了这个检验。哈夫曼的两个最罕见的、Kruskal 的最便宜的边也一样。`,"Giving change with the largest coin first works for 1, 5, 10, 25 and fails for 1, 3, 4. Before trusting a greedy rule, hunt for a small case that breaks it.":`找零时先给最大的硬币，对 1、5、10、25 有效，对 1、3、4 就不行。在相信一条贪心规则之前，先找找有没有能推翻它的小例子。`,"If one turns up":`如果找到了一个`,"Fall back on dynamic programming or backtracking: slower, but they consider every option.":`退回到动态规划或回溯：慢一些，但它们会考虑每一种选项。`},subsets:t,permutations:n,"n-queens":{"if row is past the last: a solution":`如果 row 超过了最后一行: 找到一个解`,"for each column in this row:":`对每个 这一行中的列:`,"if no queen attacks that square:":`如果 没有皇后攻击那个格子:`,"put a queen there":`在那里放一个皇后`,"take it off again        // backtrack":`再把它拿走        // 回溯`,"Four queens, no attacks":`四个皇后，互不攻击`,"Put four queens on a 4 × 4 board so that no two share a row, a column or a diagonal.":`在 4 × 4 的棋盘上放四个皇后，使任意两个都不在同一行、同一列或同一条对角线上。`,"There are 1,820 ways to put four queens on sixteen squares. Backtracking finds a good one by trying almost none of them: one queen per row, and give up on a board the moment it cannot be finished.":`在十六个格子上放四个皇后，有 1,820 种放法。回溯几乎一种都不用试就能找到一个好的：每行一个皇后，一旦某个棋盘不可能完成就立刻放弃。`,"Queens placed":`已放的皇后`,"Times backed up":`退回的次数`,"Place one, cross out what it attacks":`放一个，划掉它攻击的格子`,Place:`放置`,"Put the first queen in the first square of row 1. Cross out every square below that it attacks: its column and its diagonal.":`把第一个皇后放在第 1 行的第一个格子。划掉它下方能攻击到的每个格子：它所在的列和对角线。`,"Those squares are ruled out for good, as long as this queen stays.":`只要这个皇后还在，这些格子就永远排除了。`,"The next row":`下一行`,"Row 2 has two safe squares left. Take the first, c, and cross out what the new queen attacks.":`第 2 行还剩两个安全的格子。取第一个 c，划掉新皇后攻击的格子。`,"A dead end":`死路`,"Dead end":`死路`,"Row 3 has no safe square at all. This board can never be finished, whatever is done in row 4.":`第 3 行一个安全的格子都没有。不管第 4 行怎么放，这个棋盘都不可能完成。`,"So nothing more is tried on it. Everything that would have followed is skipped at a stroke: that is the power of backtracking.":`所以不再在它上面尝试任何东西。原本会接着发生的一切都被一笔勾销：这就是回溯的威力。`,"nowhere is safe":`没有安全的地方`,"Step back and try the next":`退一步，试下一个`,"Take the last queen off and try the next square in its row, d. Now row 3 has a safe square, b. But then row 4 has none.":`拿走最后一个皇后，试它所在行的下一个格子 d。现在第 3 行有一个安全的格子 b。但接着第 4 行一个都没有。`,"Both squares in row 2 have failed. The fault lies further back: with the very first queen.":`第 2 行的两个格子都失败了。问题出在更早的地方：就在第一个皇后身上。`,"A solution":`一个解`,"Move the first queen to b and go again: d in row 2, a in row 3, c in row 4. Four queens, none attacking another.":`把第一个皇后移到 b，再来一遍：第 2 行放 d，第 3 行放 a，第 4 行放 c。四个皇后，谁也不攻击谁。`,"It took a handful of placements, because every dead end was dropped as soon as it showed itself.":`只放了几次，因为每条死路一出现就被放弃了。`,"The pattern":`模式`,"Choose, check, go deeper; when stuck, undo the last choice and try the next. Sudoku, mazes and timetables are solved the same way.":`选择、检查、深入；卡住了就撤销上一个选择，试下一个。数独、迷宫和排课表都是这样解的。`},maze:r,memoization:i,tabulation:a,"grid-paths":{"for r from 1 to rows − 1:":`对于 r 从 1 到 rows − 1:`,"for c from 1 to cols − 1:":`对于 c 从 1 到 cols − 1:`,"return ways[last r][last c]":`返回 ways[最后的 r][最后的 c]`,"Only right, only down":`只能向右，只能向前`,"A robot stands on the back-left square of a 3 × 4 grid. It can step one square right or one square forward, never back. How many different routes take it to the opposite corner?":`一个机器人站在 3 × 4 网格左后方的格子上。它每步可以向右或向前走一格，从不后退。有多少条不同的路线能把它带到对角？`,"Start with what is certain: there is exactly one way to be where it already is.":`先从确定的开始：待在它已经在的地方，正好有一种方式。`,start:`起点`,Grid:`网格`,"Squares filled":`已填格子`,"Routes to the far corner":`到对角的路线数`,"The edges are easy":`边上很简单`,"Along the back row the robot can only have kept going right. Along the left column it can only have kept coming forward.":`沿着最后面那一排，机器人只可能一直向右走。沿着最左边那一列，它只可能一直向前走。`,"One route to each of those squares.":`到这些格子都只有一条路线。`,"Arrive from behind or from the left":`从后面或从左边来`,"Any other square can be entered in only two ways: from the square behind it, or from the square to its left.":`其他任何格子都只有两种进入方式：从它后面的格子，或者从它左边的格子。`,"So the routes to it are the routes to those two, added together. For this square, 1 + 1 = 2.":`所以到它的路线数，就是到这两个格子的路线数之和。对这个格子来说，1 + 1 = 2。`,"Fill the row":`填满这一排`,"Carry on along the row. Each square adds the one behind it and the one to its left, both already filled in.":`沿着这一排继续。每个格子把它后面的和左边的加起来，两个都已经填好了。`,"2 + 1 = 3, then 3 + 1 = 4.":`2 + 1 = 3，然后 3 + 1 = 4。`,"The far corner":`对角`,"The front row goes the same way: 3, then 6, then the corner: 4 from behind plus 6 from the left.":`最前面一排也一样：3，然后 6，然后是对角：后面的 4 加上左边的 6。`,"Ten routes.":`十条路线。`,"One table, many questions":`一张表，很多问题`,"Each square was filled once, from two neighbours. The same table handles the usual twists.":`每个格子只填一次，由两个邻居得出。同一张表还能处理常见的变化。`,"A blocked square simply gets 0. If squares have costs and you want the cheapest route, take the <em>smaller</em> of the two neighbours instead of adding them.":`被挡住的格子直接填 0。如果格子有代价，而你想要最便宜的路线，就取两个邻居中<em>较小</em>的那个，而不是把它们相加。`,"O(rows × columns) time. Only the previous row is ever read, so one row of memory is enough.":`O(行数 × 列数) 时间。只会读取前一行，所以一行的内存就够了。`},knapsack:o,"coin-change":{"for a from 1 to amount:":`对于 a 从 1 到 amount:`,"fewest[a] ← 1 + the smallest of fewest[a − c],":`fewest[a] ← 1 + fewest[a − c] 中最小的，`,"over every coin c that is not bigger than a":`c 取所有不大于 a 的硬币`,"return fewest[amount]":`返回 fewest[amount]`,"Making change":`找零`,"When greedy goes wrong":`贪心出错的时候`,"With coins worth 1, 3 and 4, what is the fewest needed to make 6? The obvious method, biggest coin first, gives 4 + 1 + 1: three coins. But 3 + 3 does it in two.":`用面值 1、3 和 4 的硬币，凑出 6 最少需要几枚？显而易见的方法是先用最大的硬币，得到 4 + 1 + 1：三枚。但 3 + 3 只要两枚。`,"Being greedy does not always work. Dynamic programming does: work out the answer for every smaller amount first. Making 0 takes no coins.":`贪心并不总是管用。动态规划管用：先算出每个更小金额的答案。凑出 0 不需要硬币。`,Coins:`硬币`,Amount:`金额`,"Fewest coins":`最少硬币数`,"Build up from below":`从下往上搭`,"For 1 and 2, only the 1-coin fits. So the answer is one coin plus the answer for one less.":`对 1 和 2，只有 1 元硬币放得进去。所以答案是一枚硬币加上少一元时的答案。`,"Try every last coin":`试遍每种最后一枚硬币`,"For 3 there is a choice. If the last coin is a 1, the rest is 2, which needs two coins: three in all. If the last coin is a 3, the rest is 0: one coin.":`对 3 就有选择了。如果最后一枚是 1，剩下的是 2，需要两枚：一共三枚。如果最后一枚是 3，剩下的是 0：一枚。`,"Whatever the best way is, it ends with <em>some</em> coin. Try each, and keep the best.":`不管最好的方法是什么，它都以<em>某枚</em>硬币结束。每种都试一下，保留最好的。`,"Each cell reads back":`每个格子都往回读`,"4 is a single coin. 5 looks back by 1, by 3 and by 4, at the cells for 4, 2 and 1, and takes the smallest: 4 and then 1.":`4 是单独一枚硬币。5 往回看 1、3 和 4，也就是 4、2 和 1 的格子，取最小的：4 然后 1。`,"Every cell is filled the same way, from cells already known.":`每个格子都是用同样的方法，从已知的格子填出来的。`,"The case greedy missed":`贪心错过的情况`,"6 looks back at 5, 3 and 2, which need 2, 1 and 2 coins. The best is through 3: one more coin makes two. That is 3 + 3.":`6 往回看 5、3 和 2，它们分别需要 2、1 和 2 枚。最好的是经过 3：再加一枚就是两枚。也就是 3 + 3。`,"Nothing was assumed about which coin is best. Every option was simply checked.":`没有预设哪枚硬币最好。每个选项都只是检查了一遍。`,"Greedy would have used three.":`贪心会用三枚。`,"Any amount":`任意金额`,"7 is two coins as well, 3 + 4. The table can go on as far as is needed.":`7 也是两枚，3 + 4。这张表需要多长都可以继续下去。`,"A greedy choice is quick and sometimes wrong. A table of subproblems is a little slower and always right.":`贪心的选择很快，有时会错。子问题表稍微慢一点，但总是对的。`,"O(amount × number of coins).":`O(金额 × 硬币种类数)。`},"longest-increasing-subsequence":{"for each j before i:":`对每个 i 之前的 j:`,"if a[j] < a[i]:":`如果 a[j] < a[i]:`,"longest[i] ← the larger of":`longest[i] ← 以下两者中较大的`,"longest[i] and longest[j] + 1":`longest[i] 和 longest[j] + 1`,"return the largest value in longest":`返回 longest 中的最大值`,"Rising, with gaps allowed":`递增，允许跳过`,"Pick numbers from this row, left to right, so that each is bigger than the one before. You may skip as many as you like. How long can the run be?":`从这一排里从左到右挑数，让每个都比前一个大。想跳过多少个都行。这串数最长能有多长？`,"3, 4, 5 is one such run. Trying every possible selection means 2ⁿ of them.":`3、4、5 就是这样的一串。试遍每种可能的挑法，就是 2ⁿ 种。`,"The numbers":`这些数`,"of 5":`/ 5`,"The best run ending here":`以这里结尾的最长一串`,"Ask a smaller question of each cell: what is the longest rising run that <strong>ends at this number</strong>?":`对每个格子问一个更小的问题：<strong>以这个数结尾</strong>的最长递增串有多长？`,"For 3 it is just itself: 1. For 1 there is nothing smaller before it to follow, so also 1.":`对 3 来说，就是它自己：1。对 1 来说，它前面没有更小的数可以接在后面，所以也是 1。`,"nothing smaller before":`前面没有更小的`,"Follow something smaller":`接在更小的后面`,"4 can come after any smaller number to its left. Both 3 and 1 are smaller, and each ends a run of length 1.":`4 可以接在它左边任何一个更小的数后面。3 和 1 都更小，而且各自都结束一串长度为 1 的。`,"Follow either one and the run is 1 + 1 = 2.":`接在任何一个后面，这一串都是 1 + 1 = 2。`,"Only the smaller ones count":`只有更小的才算`,"2 cannot follow 3 or 4: they are bigger. It can follow 1, which gives 1 + 1 = 2.":`2 不能接在 3 或 4 后面：它们更大。它可以接在 1 后面，得到 1 + 1 = 2。`,"after 1 only":`只能接在 1 后面`,"Take the best of them":`取其中最好的`,"5 is bigger than everything before it, so it can follow any of them. The best runs to follow are the two of length 2.":`5 比它前面的所有数都大，所以可以接在任何一个后面。可接的最好的串是那两个长度为 2 的。`,"The biggest number in the row":`这一排中最大的数`,"The answer is the largest value in the back row: 3. It need not be in the last cell.":`答案是后面一排里的最大值：3。它不一定在最后一个格子里。`,"One such run is 3, 4, 5. Each cell looked back at every cell before it: two loops, one inside the other.":`这样的一串是 3、4、5。每个格子都回头看了它前面的每个格子：两重循环，一个套在另一个里面。`,"O(n²) like this. A cleverer version with binary search gets it down to O(n log n).":`这样做是 O(n²)。用二分查找的更巧妙的版本能把它降到 O(n log n)。`,"One longest run: 3, 4, 5.":`一个最长的串：3、4、5。`},sequences:s,"edit-distance":{"for each i, and each j:":`对每个 i 和每个 j:`,"edits[i][j] ← 1 + the smallest of":`edits[i][j] ← 1 + 以下三者中最小的`,"edits[i − 1][j]         // delete":`edits[i − 1][j]         // 删除`,"edits[i][j − 1]         // insert":`edits[i][j − 1]         // 插入`,"edits[i − 1][j − 1]     // replace":`edits[i − 1][j − 1]     // 替换`,"return edits[last i][last j]":`返回 edits[最后的 i][最后的 j]`,"How far apart are two words?":`两个词相差多远？`,"Turn SEA into EAT using three kinds of change: delete a letter, insert a letter, or replace one with another. The fewest changes needed is the <strong>edit distance</strong>.":`用三种修改把 SEA 变成 EAT：删除一个字母、插入一个字母，或者把一个字母替换成另一个。所需的最少修改次数就是<strong>编辑距离</strong>。`,"The table has a cell for every pair of beginnings. The edges are easy: turning nothing into EAT takes three inserts, and turning SEA into nothing takes three deletes.":`这张表为每一对开头部分准备了一个格子。边上很简单：从空变成 EAT 要插入三次，从 SEA 变成空要删除三次。`,"Spell checkers, “did you mean…”, comparing files, matching DNA.":`拼写检查器、“你是不是要找……”、文件比较、DNA 比对。`,From:`从`,To:`到`,"Edits needed":`需要的修改次数`,"When the letters differ":`字母不同时`,"S into E. The letters differ, so one change is needed, on top of the cheapest of three smaller problems: the cell above (delete), the cell to the left (insert), or the cell diagonally back (replace).":`S 变成 E。字母不同，所以需要一次修改，再加上三个更小问题中最便宜的那个：上面的格子（删除）、左边的格子（插入），或者斜后方的格子（替换）。`,"The cheapest of those is 0, so the answer is 1: replace S with E.":`其中最便宜的是 0，所以答案是 1：把 S 替换成 E。`,"When they match":`字母相同时`,"SE into E. The last letters are the same, so that letter costs nothing. The answer is whatever it took before it: the cell diagonally back, 1.":`SE 变成 E。最后的字母相同，所以这个字母不花任何代价。答案就是它之前所需的：斜后方的格子，1。`,"That 1 was “delete the S”, and it still is.":`那个 1 是“删除 S”，现在仍然是。`,"E = E: still 1":`E = E：仍是 1`,"The whole table":`整张表`,"The last cell covers both whole words. A and T differ, so it is 1 plus the smallest of its three neighbours, which is the 1 to its left.":`最后一个格子涵盖两个完整的词。A 和 T 不同，所以它是 1 加上三个邻居中最小的，也就是它左边的 1。`,"SEA becomes EAT in two changes.":`SEA 经过两次修改变成 EAT。`,"Which two changes":`哪两次修改`,"Walk back from the corner, each time to the cell the answer came from. A step left is an insert, a step up a delete, a diagonal step a match or a replace.":`从角上往回走，每次都走到答案来自的那个格子。往左一步是插入，往上一步是删除，斜着一步是匹配或替换。`,"Left: insert T. Then two matches, A and E. Then up: delete S. Two changes, and the table has said which.":`往左：插入 T。然后两次匹配，A 和 E。然后往上：删除 S。两次修改，而表已经说明了是哪两次。`,"delete S, insert T":`删除 S，插入 T`},"bits-and-masks":{"mask ← only bit k switched on":`mask ← 只打开第 k 位`,"return (x AND mask) is not 0":`返回 (x AND mask) 是否不为 0`,"return x OR mask":`返回 x OR mask`,"return x AND (NOT mask)":`返回 x AND (NOT mask)`,"return x XOR mask":`返回 x XOR mask`,"A number is a row of switches":`数字是一排开关`,"Inside the machine every number is a row of <strong>bits</strong>: switches that are on or off. Each is worth twice the one to its right: 1, 2, 4, 8 and so on.":`在机器内部，每个数字都是一排<strong>位</strong>：开着或关着的开关。每一位的值都是它右边那一位的两倍：1、2、4、8，依此类推。`,"A block means the bit is on. Here that is 32, 8, 4 and 1, so this byte holds 45. The empty row behind is for a second number.":`方块表示这一位是开着的。这里是 32、8、4 和 1，所以这个字节存的是 45。后面那一排空的是给第二个数用的。`,mask:`掩码`,"A mask points at one bit":`掩码指向一个位`,Test:`检查`,"To ask about a single bit, make a second number with only that bit on: a <strong>mask</strong>.":`要问某一位的情况，就做第二个数，只打开那一位：这就是<strong>掩码</strong>。`,"<strong>AND</strong> keeps a bit only where both rows have one. The 8 bit is on in both, so something survives: the bit is set.":`<strong>AND</strong> 只在两排都有的地方保留一位。8 这一位在两排里都开着，所以有东西留下来：这一位是置位的。`,"on in both":`两排都开着`,"not 0: the bit is on":`不为 0：这一位是开着的`,"OR switches a bit on":`OR 打开一位`,"Now a mask with only the 64 bit. <strong>OR</strong> gives a 1 wherever either row has one.":`现在是一个只有 64 这一位的掩码。<strong>OR</strong> 在任意一排有 1 的地方都给出 1。`,"The 64 bit comes on and nothing else is touched. 45 becomes 109.":`64 这一位打开了，其他什么都没碰。45 变成 109。`,"AND with the opposite switches it off":`和反面做 AND 就把它关掉`,Clear:`清除`,"To switch the 4 bit off, the mask is turned inside out: every bit on <em>except</em> the 4. Then AND.":`要关掉 4 这一位，就把掩码里外翻转：除了 4 <em>以外</em>的每一位都打开。然后做 AND。`,"Every block in front has one behind it apart from the 4, so that is the only one to go. 109 becomes 105.":`前面每个方块后面都有一个，只有 4 没有，所以只有它被去掉。109 变成 105。`,"XOR flips":`XOR 翻转`,Toggle:`切换`,"<strong>XOR</strong> gives a 1 where the two rows differ. Wherever the mask has a 1, the bit in front turns over.":`<strong>XOR</strong> 在两排不同的地方给出 1。掩码中是 1 的地方，前面那一位就会翻转。`,"This mask has the 2 and the 1. The 2 bit comes on, the 1 bit goes off. 105 becomes 106.":`这个掩码有 2 和 1。2 这一位打开，1 这一位关掉。105 变成 106。`,"both flipped":`两位都翻转了`,"Eight answers in a byte":`一个字节里的八个答案`,"Each of these is a single machine instruction, and takes the same time whatever the number.":`这些操作每个都只是一条机器指令，不管数字是多少，花的时间都一样。`,"That makes bits ideal for flags: file permissions, feature switches, which keys are held down. One 64-bit number holds sixty-four yes-or-no answers.":`这让位非常适合做标志：文件权限、功能开关、哪些键被按住了。一个 64 位的数能存六十四个“是或否”的答案。`,"O(1) for every operation here.":`这里的每个操作都是 O(1)。`,Set:`置位`},"bit-tricks":{"return x << 1":`返回 x << 1`,"return x >> 1":`返回 x >> 1`,"while x is not 0:":`当 x 不为 0:`,"x ← x AND (x − 1)     // drops the lowest 1":`x ← x AND (x − 1)     // 去掉最低的 1`,"return x is not 0 and (x AND (x − 1)) = 0":`返回 x 不为 0 且 (x AND (x − 1)) = 0`,"Every place is worth double":`每一位的值都是两倍`,"This is 5: the 4 bit and the 1 bit. Each place in the row is worth twice the place to its right.":`这是 5：4 这一位和 1 这一位。这一排中每个位置的值都是它右边位置的两倍。`,"So moving the bits along the row does arithmetic. The row behind is spare for now.":`所以沿着这一排移动这些位就是在做算术。后面那一排暂时空着。`,Trick:`技巧`,Gives:`得到`,"Shift left to double":`左移就是翻倍`,"<strong>x &lt;&lt; 1</strong> slides every bit one place to the left. Each lands on a place worth twice as much, so the whole number doubles: 10.":`<strong>x &lt;&lt; 1</strong> 把每一位向左滑一个位置。每一位都落到值是两倍的位置上，所以整个数翻倍：10。`,"Shifting k places multiplies by 2ᵏ.":`移动 k 个位置就是乘以 2ᵏ。`,"Shift right to halve":`右移就是减半`,"<strong>x &gt;&gt; 1</strong> slides everything back to the right. Every bit is worth half what it was: 10 becomes 5.":`<strong>x &gt;&gt; 1</strong> 把所有位滑回右边。每一位的值都是原来的一半：10 变成 5。`,"What falls off the end":`从末端掉下去的东西`,"Shift right once more. The 1 bit has nowhere to go, and is dropped. 5 becomes 2: halved, with the remainder thrown away.":`再右移一次。1 这一位无处可去，被丢掉了。5 变成 2：减半，余数扔掉。`,"That last bit says whether a number is odd. <strong>x AND 1</strong> reads it, and is the quickest odd-or-even test there is.":`最后这一位说明一个数是不是奇数。<strong>x AND 1</strong> 读取它，这是最快的奇偶检查。`,"The remainder, 1, is lost.":`余数 1 丢掉了。`,"One less than a number":`比一个数少一`,"A new number: 12, which is 8 + 4. Behind it stands 12 − 1 = 11.":`一个新数：12，也就是 8 + 4。它后面站着 12 − 1 = 11。`,"Subtracting 1 always does the same thing to the bits. The lowest 1 goes off, and every 0 below it comes on. Everything above stays as it was.":`减去 1 对这些位做的事总是一样的。最低的 1 关掉，它下面的每个 0 都打开。上面的一切保持原样。`,"the lowest 1":`最低的 1`,"AND them, and the lowest 1 is gone":`把它们 AND 起来，最低的 1 就没了`,"Now <strong>x AND (x − 1)</strong>. Above the lowest 1 the two rows match, so those bits survive. From the lowest 1 down they never both have a block.":`现在做 <strong>x AND (x − 1)</strong>。在最低的 1 上面，两排是一样的，所以那些位保留下来。从最低的 1 往下，两排从不同时有方块。`,"Exactly one bit disappears: 12 becomes 8.":`正好消失一位：12 变成 8。`,"Two things that buys":`这能带来的两样好处`,"To count the 1s in a number, keep knocking off the lowest until nothing is left. The loop runs once per 1, not once per bit.":`要数一个数里有几个 1，就不断去掉最低的那个，直到什么都不剩。循环每个 1 跑一次，而不是每一位跑一次。`,"A power of two has exactly one bit on. So x is a power of two when knocking that bit off leaves 0, as it would here.":`2 的幂恰好只有一位是开着的。所以当去掉那一位后剩下 0 时，x 就是 2 的幂，就像这里这样。`,"Compilers already turn × 2 and ÷ 2 into shifts. Write the arithmetic you mean, and keep these for when bits are the point.":`编译器本来就会把 × 2 和 ÷ 2 变成移位。写出你想表达的算术，把这些技巧留到真正和位打交道的时候用。`,"So 8 is a power of two.":`所以 8 是 2 的幂。`},bitsets:c,"p-vs-np":{"total ← add up the roads along the route":`total ← 把路线上的道路加起来`,"return total ≤ budget          // one pass: quick":`返回 total ≤ budget          // 一趟：很快`,"best ← nothing":`best ← 空`,"for each order the towns could be visited in:":`对每个 访问这些城镇可能的顺序:`,"if that round trip is cheaper than best:":`如果 这一圈比 best 便宜:`,"best ← that round trip":`best ← 这一圈`,"return best                    // every order: hopeless":`返回 best                    // 每种顺序：没希望`,"The round":`这一圈`,"A delivery round":`一圈送货路线`,"A van leaves A, has to call at every town once, and come home. Which order makes the cheapest round trip?":`一辆货车从 A 出发，必须到每个城镇各一次，然后回家。哪种顺序的一圈最便宜？`,"It sounds like a shortest-path problem, and those were easy. This one is the <strong>travelling salesman problem</strong>, and it is not.":`这听起来像最短路径问题，而那些都很容易。这个是<strong>旅行商问题</strong>，它可不容易。`,Route:`路线`,"Round trips possible":`可能的环路数`,"for 4 towns":`对 4 个城镇`,"Checking an answer is quick":`检查一个答案很快`,Check:`检查`,"Someone hands you a route: A, D, B, C and home. Is it a round trip costing 21 or less? Follow it and add up: 3 + 2 + 7 + 9 = 21. Yes.":`有人给你一条路线：A、D、B、C，然后回家。它是一圈花费 21 或更少的路线吗？沿着它走，加起来：3 + 2 + 7 + 9 = 21。是的。`,"One pass along the route settles it. Checking a proposed answer is fast however many towns there are.":`沿着路线走一趟就解决了。检查一个给出的答案很快，不管有多少个城镇。`,"total 21":`总计 21`,"Finding the best is not":`找出最好的却不快`,"That route went to the nearest town each time, and it is not the best. Round the outside, A, B, C, D and home, costs 4 + 7 + 6 + 3 = 20.":`那条路线每次都去最近的城镇，而它不是最好的。沿着外圈走，A、B、C、D，然后回家，花费 4 + 7 + 6 + 3 = 20。`,"How do you know 20 cannot be beaten? Only by ruling out every other order. Every known method that guarantees the best answer takes time that explodes as towns are added.":`你怎么知道 20 不能被超越？只有把其他每种顺序都排除掉。每种保证得到最佳答案的已知方法，所需时间都会随着城镇的增加而爆炸。`,"total 20":`总计 20`,"The count explodes":`数量爆炸`,"Four towns have only 3 different round trips. Each extra town multiplies the count: 12 for five towns, 181,440 for ten.":`四个城镇只有 3 种不同的环路。每多一个城镇，数量就会成倍增加：五个城镇 12 种，十个城镇 181,440 种。`,"At twenty towns there are sixty million billion. A machine checking a billion routes a second would need about two years. At thirty towns, far longer than the age of the universe.":`二十个城镇时有六京种。一台每秒检查十亿条路线的机器大约需要两年。三十个城镇时，所需时间远远超过宇宙的年龄。`,"4 towns":`4 个城镇`,"3 round trips":`3 种环路`,"5 towns":`5 个城镇`,"10 towns":`10 个城镇`,"15 towns":`15 个城镇`,"43.6 billion":`436 亿`,"20 towns":`20 个城镇`,"60 million billion":`6 京`,"(n − 1)! ÷ 2 round trips for n towns.":`n 个城镇有 (n − 1)! ÷ 2 种环路。`,"P and NP":`P 与 NP`,"<strong>P</strong> is the class of problems that can be <em>solved</em> in polynomial time: n, n², n³. Sorting, shortest paths, spanning trees: almost everything in this course.":`<strong>P</strong> 是能在多项式时间内<em>解出</em>的问题类：n、n²、n³。排序、最短路径、生成树：这门课里几乎所有东西。`,"<strong>NP</strong> is the class whose answers can be <em>checked</em> in polynomial time. “Is there a round trip costing 20 or less?” is in NP. Everything in P is in NP too. Whether the two classes are really the same, whether quick to check always means quick to solve, is the most famous open question in computing.":`<strong>NP</strong> 是答案能在多项式时间内<em>验证</em>的问题类。“有没有花费 20 或更少的环路？”属于 NP。P 中的一切也都属于 NP。这两类是否真的相同，也就是“验证快”是否总意味着“求解快”，是计算机领域最著名的悬而未决的问题。`,Unsolved:`未解决`,"Almost everyone believes P ≠ NP. No one has proved it. There is a million-dollar prize.":`几乎所有人都相信 P ≠ NP。没有人证明过。为此设有一百万美元的奖金。`,"Knowing when to stop looking":`知道什么时候该停止寻找`,"The hardest problems in NP are called <strong>NP-complete</strong>: a fast method for any one of them would give a fast method for all. This round trip question is one. So are timetabling, packing, colouring a map, and Sudoku on large grids.":`NP 中最难的问题叫作 <strong>NP 完全</strong>问题：其中任何一个有了快速方法，所有问题就都有了快速方法。这个环路问题就是其中之一。排课表、装箱、地图着色、大棋盘上的数独也都是。`,"When a problem turns out to be one of these, stop hunting for a fast exact algorithm. Use backtracking or dynamic programming if the input is small, or settle for a method that gets close to the best quickly.":`当一个问题被证明是其中之一时，就别再找快速的精确算法了。输入小的话就用回溯或动态规划，或者退而求其次，用一种能很快接近最佳答案的方法。`,"The knapsack table from earlier is fast only while the capacity is a small number.":`前面那张背包表，只有在容量是个小数字时才快。`}};export{c as bitsets,l as default,o as knapsack,r as maze,i as memoization,n as permutations,e as quickselect,s as sequences,t as subsets,a as tabulation};